  planner_response {
    response: "I have built **AuraSafe**, a responsive three-screen frontend prototype for a Women Safety Application using React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Lucide icons, Google Fonts (`Plus Jakarta Sans`, `DM Sans`, `JetBrains Mono`), and browser `localStorage` persistence.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Three Main Screens Overview\n\n1. **Screen 1 \342\200\224 Login / Welcome**\n   - Displays the **AuraSafe** brand mark, safety tagline, editorial visual panel on desktop, and a mobile-first Sign In form.\n   - Validates **Full Name or Phone Number** (10\342\200\22315 digit phone check when numbers are entered) and **Password** (minimum 6 characters, with visibility toggle).\n   - Includes **Forgot Password** (updates the locally saved prototype account), a **Continue with Google** option with an honest OAuth integration notice, a **Fill Demo** helper (`9876543210` / `Safe@1234`), and navigation to **Create New Account**.\n   - Returning registered users remain saved in `localStorage` and can sign back in after logging out.\n\n2. **Screen 2 \342\200\224 Registration / Profile Setup**\n   - Captures all 8 required fields: **Full Name, Phone Number, Email Address, Age, Guardian Name, Guardian Phone Number, Password, and Confirm Password**, with inline validation.\n   - Includes two independent **Demo OTP Verification** sections (**User Phone OTP** and **Guardian Phone OTP**) with *Send OTP*, 6-digit code input, *Verify OTP*, verification status, and clear labelling that no real SMS is sent.\n   - Saves the profile locally, links the Guardian as the primary SOS contact, displays a confirmation summary screen, and navigates to the **Home Dashboard**.\n\n3. **Screen 3 \342\200\224 Home Dashboard**\n   - **Header & Navigation**: AuraSafe logo, personalized welcome greeting, and functional **Notifications**, **Profile**, and **Settings** triggers, paired with desktop top navigation tabs and a compact mobile thumb-zone bottom bar (`Home`, `Travel`, `Nearby`, `Assistant`, `Help`).\n   - **SOS Emergency**: High-visibility red focal card that opens the **SOS Confirmation Modal** showing registered emergency contacts, live browser GPS coordinates (when permitted), direct `tel:` dial links, and an **Emergency Alert Demonstration** payload preview.\n   - **Travel Mode**: Set starting location (manual or GPS fill), destination, and guardian contact; start tracking with a live elapsed timer, log safe check-ins, call the guardian, or end travel safely.\n   - **Threat Mode**: Calm emergency interface with a 15-second pauseable safety check countdown, optional Web Audio attention tone, direct guardian dial link, immediate SOS escalation, and **I\'m Safe \342\200\224 Cancel False Alarm**.\n   - **SOS Contact Management**: Add multiple emergency contacts, edit inline, switch primary guardian, delete contacts, or call directly.\n   - **Hands-Free Trigger Concepts**:\n     - *Shake Detection*: Enable/disable toggle, `DeviceMotionEvent` support when available, and a manual 3-tap shake test that opens SOS confirmation (never auto-dials).\n     - *Voice Activation*: Custom secret demo phrase, browser Web Speech API detection, microphone permission status, foreground listening, and manual keyword simulation.\n     - *Hand Gesture Concept*: Live camera permission & preview via `getUserMedia`, clearly marked as a Phase 2 computer-vision placeholder with an SOS confirmation flow preview.\n   - **Nearby Locations**: Toggle between **Police Stations** and **Restrooms** over a clean map integration placeholder (no fabricated addresses), optional live GPS capture, and working external Maps search/direction links.\n   - **Safety Guidance Chat (Demo Assistant)**: Clearly labelled rule-based demo assistant with welcome message, quick safety prompts, and interactive chat thread.\n   - **Help, Profile & Settings**: Regional emergency helplines (`tel:` links), safety checklist, editable Profile modal (with optional local photo upload), and Settings modal (Edit Profile, Change Password, Manage Contacts, Notification & Privacy toggles, and Log Out).\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Test Each Feature\n\n- **Login & Returning Session**: Click **Fill Demo** \342\206\222 **Sign In**, or click **Create Account** to register a new user. Log out via **Settings \342\206\222 Log Out**, then sign back in using your registered name or phone number.\n- **Demo OTP Flow**: On the Registration screen, enter valid user and guardian phone numbers, click **Send OTP** in each panel, enter the displayed 6-digit demo code, and click **Verify**.\n- **SOS & Contacts**: Click **Trigger SOS Confirmation** to test GPS permission, view guardian `tel:` call links, and run the alert demonstration. Open **SOS Contacts** to add, edit, promote, or remove contacts.\n- **Travel & Threat Modes**: Start a trip in **Travel Mode**, log a check-in, and click **End Travel**. Open **Threat Mode** to test the countdown, pause/resume, attention tone, false alarm cancellation, and SOS escalation.\n- **Smart Trigger Concepts**: Switch between **Shake**, **Voice**, and **Gesture** tabs to test the 3-shake counter, custom voice phrase/microphone test, and live camera preview.\n- **Profile, Settings & Notifications**: Use the top-right header icons to edit profile fields, upload a local avatar, change password, toggle preferences, and review logged safety events.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Running Locally & VS Code Setup\n\n1. Open the project folder in **VS Code**.\n2. Open the integrated terminal (`Ctrl + \\`` or `Cmd + \\``) and install dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n3. Start the local development server on port `3000`:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n4. Open `http://localhost:3000` in your browser (use Chrome/Edge DevTools device toolbar to inspect mobile and desktop responsiveness).\n5. Build for production anytime with:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Working Now vs. Future Backend / API Integration\n\n| Capability | Working in Round 1 Prototype | Requires Future Backend / Native API |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Accounts, Login & Profile** | LocalStorage multi-user accounts, validation, session persistence, profile edit, password change | Server database, hashed credentials, JWT/session auth |\n| **OTP & Google Sign-In** | Clearly labelled 6-digit demo OTP flow & honest OAuth notice | SMS gateway (Twilio/SNS) & Google OAuth 2.0 backend |\n| **Emergency Calling & Alerts** | Direct `tel:` dialer links, live browser GPS coordinates, alert payload demonstration | Automated SMS/WhatsApp dispatch & guardian push notifications |\n| **Travel Mode & Nearby Places** | Local trip timer, check-in log, GPS capture, external Maps search links | Live streaming GPS share links & embedded Maps/Places API |\n| **AI Assistant & Smart Triggers** | Scripted safety Q&A demo, foreground shake/speech/camera previews | Live LLM backend, always-on native background shake/voice wake-word & CV gesture model |"
    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements Progress**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the applet compilation and linting completed without issue. Now, I\'m meticulously reviewing the initial requirements, starting with the prompt. Specifically, I am cross-referencing to ensure that the three mandated screens\342\200\224Login/Welcome, and whatever else comes next\342\200\224are implemented exactly as requested, focusing on their respective components.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Scope**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the feature scope. I\'m focusing on the specifics of the login and sign-up flows. I\'m noting the tagline, the Sign In/Create Account buttons, Google Sign-In with an honest OAuth notice, and password visibility toggle. I\'m also ensuring the \"Forgot Password\" modal, plus name/phone and password validation are implemented. I\'m also addressing the demo credentials. Finally, I am currently working on LocalStorage persistence for returning users.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Detail**\n\nI\'m now detailing more features. I\'ve broken down: travel status indicators, threat mode, and SOS emergency features. I am defining SOS contact setup, the help section, and settings options. I am also working through the profile and nearby location features, including map integration. I\'ve focused on UI components for an emergency, for SOS contacts, and for safety controls.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Ja4Ba-DBC5movdIPr9-y2Qo"
    modified_response: "I have built **AuraSafe**, a responsive three-screen frontend prototype for a Women Safety Application using React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Lucide icons, Google Fonts (`Plus Jakarta Sans`, `DM Sans`, `JetBrains Mono`), and browser `localStorage` persistence.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Three Main Screens Overview\n\n1. **Screen 1 \342\200\224 Login / Welcome**\n   - Displays the **AuraSafe** brand mark, safety tagline, editorial visual panel on desktop, and a mobile-first Sign In form.\n   - Validates **Full Name or Phone Number** (10\342\200\22315 digit phone check when numbers are entered) and **Password** (minimum 6 characters, with visibility toggle).\n   - Includes **Forgot Password** (updates the locally saved prototype account), a **Continue with Google** option with an honest OAuth integration notice, a **Fill Demo** helper (`9876543210` / `Safe@1234`), and navigation to **Create New Account**.\n   - Returning registered users remain saved in `localStorage` and can sign back in after logging out.\n\n2. **Screen 2 \342\200\224 Registration / Profile Setup**\n   - Captures all 8 required fields: **Full Name, Phone Number, Email Address, Age, Guardian Name, Guardian Phone Number, Password, and Confirm Password**, with inline validation.\n   - Includes two independent **Demo OTP Verification** sections (**User Phone OTP** and **Guardian Phone OTP**) with *Send OTP*, 6-digit code input, *Verify OTP*, verification status, and clear labelling that no real SMS is sent.\n   - Saves the profile locally, links the Guardian as the primary SOS contact, displays a confirmation summary screen, and navigates to the **Home Dashboard**.\n\n3. **Screen 3 \342\200\224 Home Dashboard**\n   - **Header & Navigation**: AuraSafe logo, personalized welcome greeting, and functional **Notifications**, **Profile**, and **Settings** triggers, paired with desktop top navigation tabs and a compact mobile thumb-zone bottom bar (`Home`, `Travel`, `Nearby`, `Assistant`, `Help`).\n   - **SOS Emergency**: High-visibility red focal card that opens the **SOS Confirmation Modal** showing registered emergency contacts, live browser GPS coordinates (when permitted), direct `tel:` dial links, and an **Emergency Alert Demonstration** payload preview.\n   - **Travel Mode**: Set starting location (manual or GPS fill), destination, and guardian contact; start tracking with a live elapsed timer, log safe check-ins, call the guardian, or end travel safely.\n   - **Threat Mode**: Calm emergency interface with a 15-second pauseable safety check countdown, optional Web Audio attention tone, direct guardian dial link, immediate SOS escalation, and **I\'m Safe \342\200\224 Cancel False Alarm**.\n   - **SOS Contact Management**: Add multiple emergency contacts, edit inline, switch primary guardian, delete contacts, or call directly.\n   - **Hands-Free Trigger Concepts**:\n     - *Shake Detection*: Enable/disable toggle, `DeviceMotionEvent` support when available, and a manual 3-tap shake test that opens SOS confirmation (never auto-dials).\n     - *Voice Activation*: Custom secret demo phrase, browser Web Speech API detection, microphone permission status, foreground listening, and manual keyword simulation.\n     - *Hand Gesture Concept*: Live camera permission & preview via `getUserMedia`, clearly marked as a Phase 2 computer-vision placeholder with an SOS confirmation flow preview.\n   - **Nearby Locations**: Toggle between **Police Stations** and **Restrooms** over a clean map integration placeholder (no fabricated addresses), optional live GPS capture, and working external Maps search/direction links.\n   - **Safety Guidance Chat (Demo Assistant)**: Clearly labelled rule-based demo assistant with welcome message, quick safety prompts, and interactive chat thread.\n   - **Help, Profile & Settings**: Regional emergency helplines (`tel:` links), safety checklist, editable Profile modal (with optional local photo upload), and Settings modal (Edit Profile, Change Password, Manage Contacts, Notification & Privacy toggles, and Log Out).\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Test Each Feature\n\n- **Login & Returning Session**: Click **Fill Demo** \342\206\222 **Sign In**, or click **Create Account** to register a new user. Log out via **Settings \342\206\222 Log Out**, then sign back in using your registered name or phone number.\n- **Demo OTP Flow**: On the Registration screen, enter valid user and guardian phone numbers, click **Send OTP** in each panel, enter the displayed 6-digit demo code, and click **Verify**.\n- **SOS & Contacts**: Click **Trigger SOS Confirmation** to test GPS permission, view guardian `tel:` call links, and run the alert demonstration. Open **SOS Contacts** to add, edit, promote, or remove contacts.\n- **Travel & Threat Modes**: Start a trip in **Travel Mode**, log a check-in, and click **End Travel**. Open **Threat Mode** to test the countdown, pause/resume, attention tone, false alarm cancellation, and SOS escalation.\n- **Smart Trigger Concepts**: Switch between **Shake**, **Voice**, and **Gesture** tabs to test the 3-shake counter, custom voice phrase/microphone test, and live camera preview.\n- **Profile, Settings & Notifications**: Use the top-right header icons to edit profile fields, upload a local avatar, change password, toggle preferences, and review logged safety events.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Running Locally & VS Code Setup\n\n1. Open the project folder in **VS Code**.\n2. Open the integrated terminal (`Ctrl + \\`` or `Cmd + \\``) and install dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n3. Start the local development server on port `3000`:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n4. Open `http://localhost:3000` in your browser (use Chrome/Edge DevTools device toolbar to inspect mobile and desktop responsiveness).\n5. Build for production anytime with:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Working Now vs. Future Backend / API Integration\n\n| Capability | Working in Round 1 Prototype | Requires Future Backend / Native API |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Accounts, Login & Profile** | LocalStorage multi-user accounts, validation, session persistence, profile edit, password change | Server database, hashed credentials, JWT/session auth |\n| **OTP & Google Sign-In** | Clearly labelled 6-digit demo OTP flow & honest OAuth notice | SMS gateway (Twilio/SNS) & Google OAuth 2.0 backend |\n| **Emergency Calling & Alerts** | Direct `tel:` dialer links, live browser GPS coordinates, alert payload demonstration | Automated SMS/WhatsApp dispatch & guardian push notifications |\n| **Travel Mode & Nearby Places** | Local trip timer, check-in log, GPS capture, external Maps search links | Live streaming GPS share links & embedded Maps/Places API |\n| **AI Assistant & Smart Triggers** | Scripted safety Q&A demo, foreground shake/speech/camera previews | Live LLM backend, always-on native background shake/voice wake-word & CV gesture model |"
