  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Package Requirements**\n\nI\'ve determined the essential packages for this implementation. I\'ll need `@google/genai@latest` which ensures compatibility with the specified Gemini models. Also, `ws` and `@types/ws` are required to establish the WebSocket server bridge for Gemini-3.8-live. The next stage involves integrating these with the existing codebase and configuring the server.\n\n\n**Clarifying Deployment Steps**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the server deployment configurations. It looks like \"start\" should be set to \"node server.ts\" in package.json for full-stack applications. For development, the \"dev\" script should remain \"tsx server.ts\". I\'ll be sure to keep the Express server outside of vite.config.ts, and instead use it in server.ts.\n\n\n**Defining Architectural Components**\n\nI\'m solidifying the architectural plan and will run package installation after the design is set. My current focus is to integrate the real-time Gemini Live API WebSocket Bridge into the full-stack architecture, ensuring it shares the Express server\'s port (3000) for seamless operation. I\'m leveraging `http.createServer(app)` to facilitate this integration and making sure the `WebSocketServer` is bound at the `/api/live-voice` path. I\'m also ensuring the `GoogleGenAI` instance is correctly configured with the necessary API key and user agent, connecting to the `gemini-3.8-live` model.\n\n\n**Formulating Feature Declarations**\n\nI\'m developing the function declarations now, crucial for voice-driven app control. I\'m focusing on defining core features. Right now, I\'m thinking of `open_sos`, `activate_threat_mode`, `deactivate_threat_mode`, `call_guardian`, `send_emergency_alert`, `share_live_location`, `open_nearby_police`, and `open_page`. I\'m also ensuring the system can handle `speechConfig`, and the empty objects `inputAudioTranscription` and `outputAudioTranscription`. I\'m starting the first phase with `open_sos`, and will build outwards from there.\n\n\n**Defining Tool Invocation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the AI will trigger application actions. I need to make sure the app handles tool calls effectively. I\'m focusing on features such as `trigger_fake_call`, and `start_safety_checkin` and how the server will forward `{ type: \"toolCall\", calls }` to the browser, and the ensuing `toolResponse`. I\'m also planning to support text commands with the same function declarations via `gemini-4-hydrogen`.\n\n\n**Refining Command Integration**\n\nI\'ve integrated `gemini-4-hydrogen` to enable function calls, so typed commands now execute application actions. I\'m focusing on features, such as \"Open SOS\" or \"Activate Threat Mode\", to ensure actions are executed. I\'ve also implemented error propagation to the client, ensuring API failures are not masked.\n\nI\'m structuring Screen 3 with separate pages for each feature, accessible via top and bottom navigation and a quick switcher. Page 1, the `HomeAboutPage.tsx`, will be dedicated to \"About Aura\".\n\n\n**Outlining Page Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing each page\'s components for the user interface. For the application\'s overview, I\'m structuring concise cards for feature navigation. I\'m focusing on \"How It Works\" with a step-by-step registration to SOS and voice control. User reviews are also in focus, which include an interactive feedback form to store the reviews in `localStorage`.\n\n\n**Designing SOS Page Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing the dedicated SOS emergency page. I\'m focusing on a prominent SOS activation control and a live emergency status tracker that dynamically updates. The SOS voice/manual workflow will show active emergency status and activation timestamp. I\'m making sure it displays the registered primary guardian and trusted guardian network list, with a direct emergency call button and alert sending functionality. The page will also include a live location sharing toggle, and show an emergency offline support status indicator.\n\n\n**Delineating Offline Features**\n\nI\'m now separating offline and online functionalities more clearly in the design. I\'ve designed the `ThreatModePage.tsx`, which now has an active/deactivate control, status indicators, and elapsed time. I\'m focusing on **Emergency Audio & Video Recording**, leveraging the browser\'s `MediaRecorder` API. I\'m ensuring audio and video recordings (with appropriate permissions and indicators) are stored locally in the browser\'s IndexedDB, for playback, sharing, and deletion. There will also be clear consent and privacy notices.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Offline Protection**\n\nI\'m now implementing the device connectivity and continuity protection features. I\'m focusing on preserving the last known GPS location, battery level, online/offline state, and active session timestamp in localStorage every few seconds during active threat mode. I\'m also ensuring the application can distinguish between different types of session interruptions and detect if a previous threat mode session ended abruptly. This will also include a \"Simulate Connectivity Drop\" test control and clear disclosures about limitations.\n\n\n**Developing New UI Functions**\n\nI\'m now integrating new features for enhanced user safety. A **Safety Check-In Timer** will trigger alerts if unanswered. I\'m also implementing a **Fake Call Feature** for user convenience, allowing customizable incoming call screens. The new **AI Voice Assistant** section is powered by `gemini-3.8-live`, and uses WebSocket for real-time interaction.\n\n\n**Finalizing Command Execution**\n\nI\'m now integrating live interruption handling and real-time audio transcript displays with live visual voice waveforms. I\'m building a complete app controller that executes commands via Gemini Function Calling, including a quick-command bar and typed command input powered by the assistant API, alongside a global floating quick voice pill button. Also, I\'m designing page 6 with a dedicated Nearby Police Stations & Restrooms Page, and page 7 with a dedicated Evidence History Page.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "4rgBa9IX5J6q2w_az9-wCw"
