  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt**\n\nI\'m now meticulously dissecting the user\'s instructions. I\'m focusing on the specifics of the prompt, attempting to understand every nuance before proceeding. My current focus is on extracting the core requirements to accurately respond and tailor my approach accordingly. I\'m considering all relevant aspects.\n\n\n**Refining Strategy and Tools**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `generate_image` workflow and zero-pill discipline into my approach. I\'ve confirmed I\'ll utilize Gemini Maps Grounding on the `gemini-4-hydrogen` server to locate police stations using Google Maps, extracting essential data. I\'m also preparing to upgrade the Gemini Live Voice Controller to handle calls to both Guardians and Police. I\'ve re-examined the attached image and instructions, focusing on the required brand name change.\n\n\n**Updating UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the specified color palette and brand name change throughout the user interface. I\'m carefully extracting the hex codes for the sage background, accent colors, and text to ensure a visually consistent and readable design, while updating the brand name to **OurSafe** where needed. This includes modifications to files like `index.html` and other relevant components, so that the metadata.json is kept intact.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Consistency**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the application of the specified color palette and typeface pairings. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual consistency across all screens, adhering strictly to the sage-green background and high-contrast red for emergency alerts. I\'ve integrated `Fraunces` for headings and brand elements, and a refined modern sans-serif for body text, creating a visually attractive and thematic experience. I\'m making sure all hex codes, especially the sage-green, are correct, and working to implement this in the frontend.\n\n\n**Integrating New Fonts**\n\nI\'m now integrating the specified font pairings, optimizing for legibility and aesthetic coherence. I\'ve incorporated `Fraunces`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, and `JetBrains Mono` into `index.html` and `src/index.css`, ensuring correct weight and display configurations. I\'m prioritizing accessibility and visual harmony within the interface. I\'m also ensuring the fonts are correctly loaded to minimize any potential rendering issues.\n\n\n**Designing the Emblem**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating the visual emblem. I\'m prioritizing a graceful silhouette of a confident woman within a protective shield and olive wreath, using deep forest olive and soft warm gold on a clean sage-cream background, with a refined vector style. The design emphasizes a dignified yet modern aesthetic. I\'m focusing on ensuring it embodies the essence of the brand.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new features into the user interface, starting with high-priority elements. I\'m focusing on a 5-column emergency number strip, a 3x2 safety modules grid, and a balanced layout for \"How OurSafe Works.\" I\'m prioritizing immediate accessibility for emergency help numbers and a clean design for community reviews, and a dedicated founder, team, and mission footer section. I\'m also preparing for the integration of the AI-powered police station numbers in Threat Mode. I will create a dedicated `/api/threat` POST endpoint.\n\n\n**Implementing Police Station Search**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `nearby-police` function in `server.ts`, leveraging `gemini-4-hydrogen` with Google Maps Grounding as specified, ensuring the correct use of tools and retrieval configurations. I am extracting and displaying clickable map links directly from the grounding chunks, and obtaining phone numbers. The server will return summary text, station details, and map links for the user. I\'m ensuring I accurately extract any verified phone numbers parsed.\n\n\n**Refining AI Voice Commands**\n\nI\'m now expanding the AI voice control\'s capabilities. I\'m focusing on enabling the system to make calls to both guardians and police through a new `call_guardian_and_police` tool. I will update `server.ts`, `HomeDashboard.tsx`, and `AiVoiceAssistantPage.tsx` accordingly to support this expanded functionality.\n\n\n**Expanding Voice Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the expanded AI voice commands. I\'m focusing on the integration of `call_guardian_and_police` and `open_sos`, triggering the \"Dual Emergency Call Dispatch Panel\" for user-initiated calls. This panel will include clickable links for both guardian and police, with clear instructions about browser security limitations. I\'m prioritizing user experience and immediate call initiation.\n\n\n"
