    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Attributes**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the generated images! The women\'s emblem and the editorial banner are both working beautifully together. I am also now looking at how to combine these new, attractive components. I\'m focusing on seamless integration, and the overall cohesive look of the final product.\n\n\n**Refining the Color Palette**\n\nI\'m making excellent progress on the color and typography design system, ensuring it\'s cohesive, legible, and true to the sage aesthetic. The canvas background is perfectly `#CDD7C1`, and the elevated card surface is crisp ivory-white. I\'m carefully considering secondary surfaces, hairlines, and accent colors to create a harmonious user interface. Ensuring I avoid any purple tones is the focus for now. I\'ve chosen deep forest charcoal for the primary text.\n\n\n**Defining UI Variables**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously defining the UI variables, establishing clear semantic classes and `@theme` tokens in `src/index.css` for a unified look. I\'ve chosen `#4B5844` and `#5F6D58` for secondary text and a vibrant `#DC2626` for emergency accents. The typography is coming together with `Fraunces` for headings, `Plus Jakarta Sans` for body text, and `JetBrains Mono` for monospace elements. Now I\'m preparing to batch edits in `src/index.css`!\n\n\n**Updating UI Details**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress implementing the branding. I\'ve integrated the **OurSafe** brand name, along with the correct fonts: Fraunces, Plus Jakarta Sans, and JetBrains Mono. I\'ve also set the body\'s background color to `#CDD7C1` and the text color to `#182215`. Furthermore, I\'ve configured the UI with the proper fonts in the `index.css` file and incorporated the wordmark, using Fraunces and a botanical olive icon, in the BrandLogo.tsx component. I\'m actively working on adding new types for AI capabilities. Finally, I\'m rebranding all AI prompts to use **OurSafe** and adding new tools.\n\n\n"
