  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Interface Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the visual and functional design, specifically polishing OurSafe\'s frontend. I\'m actively integrating the Gemini API, with `/server.ts` already handling `gemini-4-hydrogen` integration alongside Google Maps Grounding. My progress is steady.\n\n\n**Finalizing App Prototype**\n\nI am now focused on completing the transition of OurSafe to a fully functional prototype. This involves systematically removing all demo-related elements, disclaimers, and placeholders across the application to provide a seamless user experience. I\'ve concentrated on ensuring that account login and registration functions flawlessly, including real-time OTP verification, Google sign-in and password recovery; and I\'m nearing completion of this phase.\n\n\n**Implementing Real Emergency Actions**\n\nI\'m now implementing real SMS, share, and call integrations. Specifically, on SOS and Guardian alerts, I\'m integrating working `sms:`, `tel:`, `mailto:`, and `navigator.share` actions. This will allow users to send pre-filled emergency messages with live GPS coordinates, directly dial guardians or police, or share their location. I\'m also refining alert status labels for clarity, replacing demo labels with accurate statuses.\n\n\n**Integrating Real-World Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating critical features. I\'ve wired up `HomeDashboard.tsx` for real-time police AI via Gemini Maps Grounding, triggered in Threat Mode, with audio/video recording and live GPS tracking. I\'ve also removed demo labels across the application and I\'m implementing a real AI Voice Assistant using Gemini 3.8 and Gemini 4 Hydrogen, including dual guardian and police calling. I\'m unifying the aesthetic, too.\n\n\n"
