  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Pinpointing the Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the core issue: `HomeDashboard.tsx` is missing crucial props (`onFetchNearbyPoliceAi`, `nearbyPoliceResult`, etc.) when rendering `ThreatModePage`. This explains the `TypeError`. My next step is a direct update to `HomeDashboard.tsx` to fix the prop passing and include `dualCall` as well.\n\n\n**Implementing the Prop Fixes**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the prop fixes across `HomeDashboard.tsx`. Specifically, I am ensuring that the correct states and callbacks (`dualCallState`, `openDualCall`, etc.) are passed to `SosPage` and related pages. Furthermore, I am addressing the `handleExecuteVoiceCommand` functionality, adding support for voice commands like `call_guardian_and_police`, as well as applying the sage botanical theme and removing all demo labels.\n\n\n**Refining the UI/UX**\n\nI\'m deep in the UI/UX refinement. I\'m actively scrubbing all \"Demo,\" \"Prototype,\" and placeholder text from `HomeAboutPage.tsx`, `ThreatModePage.tsx`, `SosPage.tsx`, and `AiVoiceAssistantPage.tsx`. My current focus is implementing real `sms:` and `navigator.share` actions in `SosPage.tsx` for genuine SOS alerts. I\'m also planning a full brand pass across other screens. This includes implementing OurSafe branding and the Sage botanical theme with Fraunces and Plus Jakarta Sans fonts.\n\n\n"
