  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Ensuring Absolute Completeness**\n\nI\'m meticulously checking for any overlooked dependencies or inconsistencies. Specifically, I\'m ensuring the renaming of `SAMPLE_REVIEWS` to `INITIAL_REVIEWS` in `storage.ts` on line 53 is mirrored completely, by updating lines 368-383. This level of thoroughness is crucial to the integrity of the project.\n\n\n**Refining Feature Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI-driven location services within the threat mode features. Specifically, I\'ve integrated `fetchNearbyPoliceAi()` to trigger automatically upon threat mode activation within `HomeDashboard.tsx` and ensure all button functions are seamlessly wired up. Additionally, I am removing all demo indicators in `ThreatModePage.tsx`, removing all labels of demo or placeholder text. My next focus will be removing the \"Prototype Demo Account / Fill Demo\" box, \"Round 1 frontend prototype\" notices and removing the prototype labels in `LoginScreen.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Google & Theming**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user onboarding experience, specifically integrating Google sign-in for seamless authentication. I\'m prioritizing a clean, Google-style account picker or instant sign-in. Alongside that, I\'m making Forgot Password a functional flow, ensuring the sage green theme (`#CDD7C1`, `#FCFDF9`, `#2F4526`) is fully implemented across all screens. I\'m next updating the `SignupScreen.tsx` screen to implement these changes.\n\n\n**Actioning Features Realistically**\n\nI\'m now overhauling demo elements across several components to reflect real-world functionality. Specifically, I\'m replacing placeholder buttons and text in `HomeAboutPage.tsx`, `TravelModePage.tsx`, `TravelModePanel.tsx`, `NearbyPage.tsx`, and `NearbyLocationsSection.tsx` with actionable features. This includes integrating a real \"Share Route SMS\" function in travel mode, connecting the \"Nearby\" page to our AI-powered police station service, and refining theme consistency with the sage green color palette in all components. I am now updating the `EvidenceHistoryPage.tsx` screen to implement these changes, and ensure the UI is coherent with the rest of the application.\n\n\n"
