    thinking: "**Analyzing API Response**\n\nOkay, so I just got a 429 error from the `/api/threat/nearby-police` endpoint. It looks like I\'ve hit the quota limit. Gotta check the plan and billing details now. This is a bit of a roadblock, but at least I know the issue.\n\n\n**Investigating Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve got a clearer picture now; the 429 error the user reported directly links to the raw JSON displayed within that specific section, so the issue is clearly related to quota exhaustion when querying the API. I\'m focusing on why the 429 happened to begin with \342\200\224 are both Google Maps and Gemini models hitting a quota, or just Google Maps? I\'m now exploring fallback options, specifically the OpenStreetMap Overpass API and Nominatim. These offer free, real-time data for nearby police stations with addresses, phone numbers, and map links, to guarantee zero 429 errors in Threat Mode.\n\n\n"
