  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\nThe user has built **OurSafe**, an AI-powered Women Safety Application (React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + Express + Gemini Live/Hydrogen APIs).\nIn the **latest turn (Focus Mode)**, the user selected the error paragraph inside Threat Mode\'s AI Nearby Police Station section:\n- **Selected Element**: `div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > main:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > section:nth-of-type(2) > p:nth-of-type(1)` (which renders `{nearbyPoliceError}` at lines 633\342\200\223637 of `/src/components/pages/ThreatModePage.tsx`).\n- **CSS Block**: `{}` (empty \342\200\224 no CSS style changes requested).\n- **User Prompt**: `\"clear the error\"`.\n\nEarlier requests from this session (all completed and verified prior to the Focus Mode turn):\n- Rebrand app from `AuraSafe` to **`OurSafe`** (without renaming `/metadata.json`).\n- Apply botanical sage color palette sampled from the user\'s wallpaper (`#CDD7C1` canvas, `#FCFDF9` cards, `#2F4526` deep olive accent, `Fraunces` display + `Plus Jakarta Sans` body + `JetBrains Mono` mono) \342\200\224 color ONLY, not the wallpaper image.\n- Remove ALL \"demo\", \"prototype\", \"placeholder\", \"simulated\", and \"AuraSafe\" / `violet-*` clutter across every screen and modal so it functions as a complete working frontend ready for backend connection.\n- Add AI-driven nearby police station + phone number lookup in Threat Mode (auto-triggered on activation) and Nearby page, plus Dual Guardian + Police calling via AI Voice Controller (`call_guardian_and_police`, `call_police`, `open_sos`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n\n#### Skills Read\n- `/skills/system_skills/focus_mode/SKILL.md` (read in current turn)\n- `/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/references/tools_and_grounding.md` (read in current turn)\n- `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`, `/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md`, `/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/references/live_api.md` (read in earlier turns)\n\n#### Completed Prior to Current Focus Mode Turn (Verified with `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` + `restart_dev_server`)\n- Rebranded and styled all pages and modals to **OurSafe** botanical sage theme (`HomeDashboard.tsx`, `LoginScreen.tsx`, `SignupScreen.tsx`, `HomeAboutPage.tsx`, `SosPage.tsx`, `ThreatModePage.tsx`, `TravelModePage.tsx`, `AiVoiceAssistantPage.tsx`, `NearbyPage.tsx`, `EvidenceHistoryPage.tsx`, `TravelModePanel.tsx`, `NearbyLocationsSection.tsx`, `SosContactsModal.tsx`, `ProfileModal.tsx`, `SettingsModal.tsx`, `NotificationsModal.tsx`, `FakeCallModal.tsx`, `BrandLogo.tsx`, `storage.ts`).\n- Deleted unused legacy Turn 1 files (`HelpSection.tsx`, `SmartTriggersSection.tsx`, `SosEmergencyModal.tsx`, `ThreatModeModal.tsx`).\n- Fixed `TypeError: onFetchNearbyPoliceAi is not a function` by wiring `nearbyPoliceResult`, `nearbyPoliceLoading`, `nearbyPoliceError`, `fetchNearbyPoliceAi`, and `dualCallState` through `HomeDashboard.tsx` to `ThreatModePage.tsx`, `SosPage.tsx`, `AiVoiceAssistantPage.tsx`, and `NearbyPage.tsx`.\n\n#### Completed in Current Focus Mode Turn (NOT YET COMPILED/LINTED OR SERVER-RESTARTED!)\n1. **Diagnosed exact error behind `section:nth-of-type(2) > p:nth-of-type(1)`**:\n   - Tested `POST http://localhost:3000/api/threat/nearby-police` with `{\"areaQuery\":\"Chennai\"}` via `curl` and confirmed it returned HTTP 500 with raw JSON:\n     `{\"error\":\"{\\\"error\\\":{\\\"code\\\":429,\\\"message\\\":\\\"You exceeded your current quota...\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\\\"...}}\"}`\n   - Confirmed `POST /api/assistant/command` on `gemini-4-hydrogen` works normally (returned valid `call_guardian_and_police` tool call), meaning the 429 quota error was specific to `tools: [{ googleMaps: {} }]`.\n   - Confirmed OpenStreetMap Nominatim (`https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?...` with `User-Agent: OurSafeApp/1.0`) is reachable and works from the server container.\n2. **Updated `/server.ts`**:\n   - Replaced `POST /api/threat/nearby-police` with a resilient **3-tier live waterfall**:\n     - **Tier 1**: `gemini-4-hydrogen` + `tools: [{ googleMaps: {} }]` (Maps Grounding)\n     - **Tier 2**: Automatic fallback to `gemini-4-hydrogen` + `tools: [{ googleSearch: {} }]` (Google Search Grounding) using reverse-geocoded neighborhood/city name (`reverseGeocodeArea()` via Nominatim when GPS coords are provided)\n     - **Tier 3**: Automatic fallback to live OpenStreetMap Nominatim lookup (`fetchNominatimPoliceStations()`) returning real police stations, addresses, any OSM phone tags, and Google Maps pin links\n   - Added `formatFriendlyServerError()` so raw JSON 429 strings are never leaked to the client.\n3. **Updated `/src/components/HomeDashboard.tsx`**:\n   - Sanitized error handling inside `fetchNearbyPoliceAi` so raw JSON / `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` messages are replaced with a clean user-friendly message.\n\n#### Pending / Not Yet Done in Current Focus Mode Turn\n- Optional small UX polish on the selected element (`ThreatModePage.tsx` lines 633\342\200\223637): keep targeted per Focus Mode (if an error message ever appears, ensure clean readability or allow clearing it when GPS is granted / a new search runs). Note: `HomeDashboard.tsx` already clears `nearbyPoliceError` at the start of `fetchNearbyPoliceAi`, and when GPS is denied, check whether `nearbyPoliceError` needs clearing when user types a new area or clicks Retry.\n- **MUST run `compile_applet` + `lint_applet`** to verify `/server.ts` and `/src/components/HomeDashboard.tsx` changes compile cleanly.\n- **MUST run `restart_dev_server`** so the updated `/server.ts` 3-tier `/api/threat/nearby-police` route is live!\n- **MUST live-test `POST http://localhost:3000/api/threat/nearby-police`** via `curl` after restarting the dev server to prove the 429 error is completely gone and real nearby police stations + numbers + links are returned!\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- `gemini-4-hydrogen` with `tools: [{ googleMaps: {} }]` hits `429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` on the current environment\'s API quota, while `gemini-4-hydrogen` without `googleMaps` (standard function calling and `googleSearch` grounding) and OpenStreetMap Nominatim both work.\n- Overpass API (`https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter`) returned `406 Not Acceptable` without an `Accept` header, whereas Nominatim (`https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search` and `/reverse`) with `User-Agent: OurSafeApp/1.0` and `Accept: application/json` works cleanly and reliably.\n- The user\'s Focus Mode selector `div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > main:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > section:nth-of-type(2) > p:nth-of-type(1)` points directly to `{nearbyPoliceError && <p ...>{nearbyPoliceError}</p>}` in `/src/components/pages/ThreatModePage.tsx` (lines 633\342\200\223637).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Resolved earlier**: `TypeError: onFetchNearbyPoliceAi is not a function` in `ThreatModePage.tsx` -> Fixed by updating `HomeDashboard.tsx` to pass all required AI police lookup and Dual Call props.\n- **Fixed in code, awaiting server restart & live verification**: `429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` raw JSON error shown in Threat Mode\'s `section:nth-of-type(2) > p:nth-of-type(1)` when `/api/threat/nearby-police` called Gemini Maps Grounding -> Fixed in `/server.ts` via automatic 3-tier waterfall (Maps Grounding -> Reverse-Geocode + Google Search Grounding -> OpenStreetMap Nominatim) + friendly error sanitization in both `/server.ts` and `/src/components/HomeDashboard.tsx`.\n- **Abandoned approach**: Overpass API without headers returned `406 Not Acceptable`; used Nominatim `/reverse` + `/search` with `User-Agent` and `Accept: application/json` instead.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Running dev server on port 3000 is still serving the **old** `/server.ts` from before the 3-tier fallback edit \342\200\224 **it MUST be restarted** via `restart_dev_server` before testing `curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/threat/nearby-police`.\n- Do NOT make unrelated theme/style edits while in Focus Mode (`CSS 1: {}` was empty). Keep any remaining edit strictly tied to clearing/fixing the error on the targeted element and verifying the endpoint.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` in parallel** to verify zero TypeScript/build issues after the `/server.ts` and `/src/components/HomeDashboard.tsx` edits.\n2. **Call `restart_dev_server`** so the updated `/server.ts` with the 3-tier `/api/threat/nearby-police` waterfall is active on port 3000.\n3. **Verify the fix live with `curl`**:\n   - Test both area search (`{\"areaQuery\":\"Chennai\"}`) and GPS coordinate lookup (`{\"latitude\":13.0827,\"longitude\":80.2707}`) against `POST http://localhost:3000/api/threat/nearby-police`.\n   - Confirm HTTP 200 response with real `stations`, `summaryText`, and `mapLinks`, and ZERO 429 error!\n   - Also check `/server.ts` `/api/assistant/command` error handler (`formatFriendlyServerError`) if needed, though only touch if relevant.\n4. **Respond concisely to the user** explaining the cause (Google Maps Grounding quota 429 error returned raw JSON into that Threat Mode alert box) and that it is now fixed with automatic Google Search Grounding + OpenStreetMap Nominatim fallback and friendly error handling.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Focus Mode compliance**: Only modify what is strictly necessary to fix/clear the error shown in `section:nth-of-type(2) > p:nth-of-type(1)` and its backing endpoint. Do not alter unrelated UI or styling.\n- **No fabricated police numbers or addresses**: Only display real grounded / OSM phone numbers or honest `100` / `112` national emergency numbers.\n- **No `metadata.json` rename**; **no `window.alert` / `window.open`**; **server-side Gemini only**; **no demo/prototype copy**.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 96
    included_step_index_end: 202
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
