    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport fs from \'fs\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [\n      react(),\n      tailwindcss(),\n      // Copies src/assets into dist/ so root-relative URLs like\n      // \"/src/assets/images/...\" (e.g. generate_image output) still resolve\n      // in production builds. Do not remove.\n      {\n        name: \'copy-unbundled-src-assets\',\n        apply: \'build\',\n        closeBundle(error?: Error): void {\n          if (error) {\n            return;\n          }\n          const distDir = path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\');\n          const srcAssets = path.resolve(__dirname, \'src/assets\');\n          const distAssets = path.resolve(distDir, \'src/assets\');\n          if (fs.existsSync(distDir) && fs.existsSync(srcAssets)) {\n            fs.cpSync(srcAssets, distAssets, {recursive: true, force: true});\n          }\n        },\n      },\n    ],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT \342\200\223 AI-POWERED WOMEN SAFETY APPLICATION\n\n## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW\n\nAct as a Senior Frontend Developer, UI/UX Designer and Software Architect.\n\nDevelop a modern, responsive, professional Women Safety Application frontend prototype.\n\n**Project Domain:** Women Safety and Security  \n**Project Type:** AI-Powered Women Safety Application  \n**Development Phase:** Round 1 \342\200\223 Frontend Working Prototype\n\nThe immediate objective is to develop ONLY THREE MAIN SCREENS:\n\n1. Login / Sign Up\n2. Registration / Profile Setup\n3. Home Dashboard\n\nDo not develop the complete backend or all advanced AI features at this stage.\n\nThe frontend must be visually attractive, interactive, responsive and functional.\n\n## 2. TECHNOLOGY STACK\n\nUse:\n- HTML5\n- CSS3\n- JavaScript\n- Font Awesome or Lucide icons\n- Google Fonts\n- LocalStorage for prototype-level profile/session persistence.\n\nUse a clean component-based structure where possible.\n\nIf React is used, explain the setup and provide all required files. Otherwise, use plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript.\n\n## 3. SCREEN 1 \342\200\223 LOGIN PAGE\n\nWhen a user opens the application for the first time, display the Login / Welcome screen.\n\n### Design requirements\n\nCreate a premium, modern UI with:\n- Application logo and name.\n- Attractive welcome heading.\n- Short safety-related tagline.\n- Sign In button.\n- Create Account / Sign Up button.\n- Google Sign-In visual option.\n- Password visibility toggle.\n- Forgot Password option.\n\n### Sign In Form\n\nRequired fields:\n- Name or Phone Number\n- Password\n\nButtons:\n- Sign In\n- Create New Account\n\nValidation:\n- Do not allow empty fields.\n- Validate the phone number format.\n- Show clear error messages.\n- Navigate to Home after successful prototype authentication.\n\nReturning users should be able to sign in without registering again.\n\n## 4. SCREEN 2 \342\200\223 SIGN UP / REGISTRATION PAGE\n\nWhen the user selects Create Account, display the registration form.\n\n### Required input fields\n\n1. Full Name\n2. Phone Number\n3. Email Address\n4. Age\n5. Guardian Name\n6. Guardian Phone Number\n7. Password\n8. Confirm Password\n\n### OTP Verification\n\nInclude separate verification sections for:\n\n- User Phone Number\n- Guardian Phone Number\n\nProvide:\n- Send OTP button.\n- OTP input field.\n- Verify OTP button.\n- Verification status.\n\nFor this frontend prototype, implement a clearly labelled demo OTP flow. Do not pretend that real SMS verification is working.\n\n### Account Creation\n\nAfter successful demo validation:\n\n- Create the profile.\n- Save the prototype profile information.\n- Allow the user to continue to the Home Dashboard.\n- Show a successful registration message.\n\nAlso provide an option to continue with Google, but clearly indicate that real Google authentication requires backend/OAuth integration.\n\n## 5. SCREEN 3 \342\200\223 HOME DASHBOARD\n\nAfter successful Login or Registration, display the main Home Dashboard.\n\nThis is the most important screen.\n\n### Dashboard Header\n\nInclude:\n- Application logo.\n- Welcome message with user\'s name.\n- Profile icon.\n- Notification icon.\n- Settings icon.\n\n### Main Dashboard Features\n\nCreate attractive interactive cards for the following features.\n\n**A. Travel Mode**\n\nPurpose:\nHelp users share their journey with trusted contacts.\n\nFrontend interactions:\n- Start Travel button.\n- Destination input.\n- Starting location.\n- Guardian contact selection.\n- Travel status indicator.\n- End Travel button.\n\n**B. Threat Mode**\n\nPurpose:\nProvide an easy way to access emergency assistance when the user feels unsafe.\n\nFrontend interactions:\n- Activate Threat Mode.\n- Display an emergency interface.\n- Show a safety check.\n- Provide an SOS option.\n- Allow the user to cancel a false alarm.\n\n**C. SOS Emergency**\n\nCreate a highly visible SOS button.\n\nWhen clicked:\n1. Display an emergency confirmation interface.\n2. Show the registered guardian contact.\n3. Display the current location if location permission is available.\n4. Provide an emergency call action.\n5. Provide an emergency alert demonstration.\n\nAllow users to add and manage SOS contacts.\n\n### SOS Contact Setup\n\nProvide:\n- Add SOS Number button.\n- Guardian Name.\n- Guardian Phone Number.\n- Save Contact button.\n- Edit and Delete options.\n\nAllow the user to add more than one emergency contact.\n\n### D. Help Section\n\nInclude:\n- Emergency assistance information.\n- Safety instructions.\n- Important emergency contacts.\n- Quick access to emergency options.\n\n### E. Settings\n\nInclude:\n- Edit Profile.\n- Change Password UI.\n- Manage Emergency Contacts.\n- Notification Preferences.\n- Privacy Settings.\n- Logout.\n\n### F. Profile\n\nWhen the user clicks the profile icon, show:\n\n- Profile Photo placeholder.\n- Full Name.\n- Phone Number.\n- Email.\n- Age.\n- Guardian Name.\n- Guardian Phone Number.\n- Edit Profile option.\n\n### G. Nearby Locations\n\nCreate a dedicated section within the Home Dashboard.\n\nInclude:\n- Find Nearby Police Stations.\n- Find Nearby Restrooms.\n\nDisplay location cards with:\n- Place Name.\n- Distance when available.\n- Address.\n- Directions button.\n\nUse a map integration placeholder if an actual Maps API is not configured. Do not invent nearby locations.\n\n### H. AI Chat Assistant\n\nCreate an AI Assistant interface within the Home Dashboard.\n\nInclude:\n- Chat input.\n- Send button.\n- Chat message display.\n- Welcome message.\n- Safety-related quick questions.\n\nFor now, use a clearly labelled demo response system. Do not claim a real AI model is connected.\n\n## 6. ADDITIONAL SAFETY INTERACTION CONCEPTS\n\nThese are planned features that should have frontend demonstration interfaces.\n\n### A. Shake Detection\n\nConcept:\nIf the user shakes the phone three times, the application should recognize the gesture and initiate an SOS confirmation flow.\n\nFor the prototype:\n- Add a Shake Detection setting.\n- Show its enabled/disabled status.\n- Provide a test-shake demonstration.\n- Use device motion events only when supported and permitted.\n- Provide a manual fallback.\n\nImportant: Do not automatically place emergency calls without user confirmation. A browser prototype cannot guarantee reliable background shake detection.\n\n### B. Voice Activation\n\nConcept:\nThe user can configure a secret emergency phrase or keyword.\n\nWhen the phrase is recognized, the app should open the emergency confirmation interface.\n\nFor the prototype:\n- Create a Voice Activation settings section.\n- Provide a microphone button.\n- Show microphone permission status.\n- Allow the user to configure a demo keyword.\n- Clearly indicate whether speech recognition is supported.\n\nDo not claim continuous background listening.\n\n### C. Hand Gesture Concept\n\nConcept:\nRecognize a predefined hand gesture using the phone camera.\n\nFor the prototype:\n- Create a gesture demonstration interface.\n- Add a camera permission request.\n- Show the camera preview when permission is granted.\n- Display a placeholder for future hand gesture recognition.\n\nDo not claim that gesture recognition is functional unless an actual recognition model is implemented.\n\n## 7. NAVIGATION STRUCTURE\n\nKeep the application limited to three main screens.\n\nScreen 1: Login / Sign Up\n\nScreen 2: Registration / Profile Setup\n\nScreen 3: Home Dashboard\n\nOther features such as Profile, Settings, SOS Contacts, Travel Mode, Threat Mode and AI Chat should open as modals, drawers, tabs or dashboard sections rather than creating unnecessary separate main screens.\n\n## 8. UI/UX DESIGN REQUIREMENTS\n\nDesign style:\n- Premium and modern.\n- Clean layout.\n- Professional application appearance.\n- Mobile-first responsive design.\n- Smooth transitions and animations.\n- Rounded cards.\n- Consistent spacing.\n- Clear typography.\n- Easy navigation.\n\nUse a safety-oriented colour palette:\n- Purple / Violet as the primary colour.\n- White backgrounds.\n- Soft lavender surfaces.\n- Red only for emergency actions.\n- Dark text for readability.\n\nAvoid:\n- Overcrowded layouts.\n- Too many unnecessary buttons.\n- Excessive animations.\n- Generic template appearance.\n- Non-functional buttons.\n\nThe Home Dashboard must look like a real, professionally designed mobile application.\n\n## 9. FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\nEvery visible button must have an appropriate action.\n\nImplement:\n- Navigation between the three main screens.\n- Sign In form validation.\n- Sign Up form validation.\n- Demo OTP verification.\n- Profile creation.\n- Profile editing.\n- Session persistence for prototype login.\n- Logout.\n- SOS contact management.\n- Travel Mode interactions.\n- Threat Mode interactions.\n- SOS confirmation interface.\n- Dashboard navigation.\n- Modal opening and closing.\n- Responsive mobile navigation.\n\nUse browser-supported capabilities appropriately.\n\nImportant technical limitations:\n- Actual phone calls require a user-triggered telephone link such as tel:.\n- Actual SMS and WhatsApp alerts require appropriate integrations.\n- Actual OTP requires an SMS provider/backend.\n- Actual Google authentication requires OAuth.\n- Actual AI chat requires an AI API/backend.\n- Real location search requires a location/maps integration.\n\nNever show a fake success message for an integration that is not connected.\n\n## 10. PROJECT FILE STRUCTURE\n\nFor a plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript implementation, organize the project as:\n\nwomen-safety-app/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.html\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 signup.html\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 home.html\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 css/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 style.css\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 signup.css\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 home.css\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 js/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 auth.js\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 signup.js\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 dashboard.js\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.js\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 assets/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 logo.png\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 icons/\n\nYou may adjust the structure if a better architecture is required.\n\n## 11. DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTIONS\n\nFollow this order:\n\nSTEP 1: Build the Login Page.\n\nSTEP 2: Build the Registration Page.\n\nSTEP 3: Build the Home Dashboard.\n\nSTEP 4: Connect navigation between all three screens.\n\nSTEP 5: Implement frontend interactions.\n\nSTEP 6: Test every button and form.\n\nSTEP 7: Test responsive layouts on mobile and desktop.\n\nSTEP 8: Fix errors and provide the final working project.\n\n## 12. FINAL OUTPUT EXPECTATIONS\n\nProvide:\n\n1. Complete source code.\n2. All required HTML files.\n3. All CSS files.\n4. All JavaScript files.\n5. Proper folder structure.\n6. Installation and running instructions.\n7. VS Code setup instructions.\n8. Explanation of each screen.\n9. Explanation of how to test each feature.\n10. A list of features that work now and features requiring backend/API integration later.\n\nDo not provide incomplete code or isolated snippets.\n\nDo not skip any of the three main screens.\n\nDo not change the application concept or remove the requested fields and features.\n\nIf any technical limitation exists, explain it and implement the best working frontend alternative.\n\n**FINAL GOAL: Build a complete, professional, interactive and responsive three-screen Women Safety Application frontend prototype that can be opened and demonstrated in a browser.**"
    }
