      text: "# ADDITIONAL FEATURES AND REQUIREMENTS \342\200\223 AI-POWERED WOMEN SAFETY APPLICATION\n\n## 1. AI Voice Assistant \342\200\223 Complete App Control\n\nIntegrate an intelligent AI Voice Assistant that allows users to control the application using voice commands, especially during emergency situations.\n\nThe AI Assistant should be able to understand and execute commands such as:\n\n- \"Open SOS\"\n- \"Activate Threat Mode\"\n- \"Call My Guardian\"\n- \"Send Emergency Alert\"\n- \"Share My Live Location\"\n- \"Open Nearby Police Stations\"\n- \"Deactivate Threat Mode\"\n\n### SOS Voice Command Workflow\n\nWhen the user says \"Open SOS\":\n\n1. The AI Assistant should recognize the voice command.\n2. Open the SOS emergency interface.\n3. Identify the registered guardian\'s phone number.\n4. Initiate an emergency call to the guardian after appropriate confirmation or an explicitly configured emergency action.\n5. Send an emergency alert message containing the user\'s available location information to registered emergency contacts.\n6. Provide an option to contact the nearest police station.\n7. Display the current emergency status to the user.\n\nThe AI Assistant should also support manual SOS activation.\n\n**Important:** The AI Assistant must act as an application controller, not just a chatbot. It should be able to navigate to the requested sections and trigger supported application functions.\n\n## 2. Home Page \342\200\223 About the Application\n\nWhen the user selects the Home section, display a dedicated Home page containing information about the application.\n\nThe Home page should include:\n\n### About the App\n- Application introduction.\n- Main purpose and vision.\n- Problems the application aims to solve.\n- How the application improves women\'s safety.\n\n### Application Features\nDisplay an overview of all major safety features with short descriptions.\n\n### How It Works\nExplain the application workflow step by step, including registration, emergency contact setup, Travel Mode, Threat Mode and SOS activation.\n\n### User Reviews and Testimonials\n- Display user reviews.\n- Provide ratings.\n- Allow users to submit feedback.\n\nUse clearly labelled sample reviews for the prototype. Do not present fictional testimonials as genuine customer reviews.\n\n### Founder and Team Details\nDisplay:\n- Founder\'s name.\n- Founder\'s introduction.\n- Project team details.\n- Project vision and mission.\n\nUse editable placeholders until the actual details are provided.\n\n### Emergency Help Numbers\nProvide a dedicated emergency assistance section displaying important emergency contact numbers, including:\n\n- Emergency Response: 112\n- Women Helpline: 181\n- Police: 100\n- Ambulance: 108\n- Child Helpline: 1098\n\nProvide a direct calling option where supported.\n\n## 3. Separate Feature Pages and Navigation\n\nEvery major feature must have its own dedicated interface and functionality.\n\nDo not combine unrelated features into one page.\n\nFor example:\n\n- Travel Mode should display only Travel Mode-related information and controls.\n- Threat Mode should display only Threat Mode-related information and controls.\n- SOS should display emergency-related actions.\n- AI Assistant should provide voice-based application control.\n- Home should display application information, features, reviews, founder details and emergency numbers.\n\nMaintain a clean and organized navigation structure.\n\n## 4. Threat Mode \342\200\223 Intelligent Emergency Protection\n\nDevelop a dedicated Threat Mode designed to help users during potentially dangerous situations.\n\nWhen Threat Mode is activated, the application should:\n\n### A. Emergency Recording\n\n- Provide an option to start audio recording.\n- Provide an option to start video recording.\n- Display recording status clearly.\n- Store recordings securely when supported.\n- Provide an emergency evidence-sharing option for authorized guardian contacts.\n\nRecording must respect device permissions, applicable privacy laws and platform restrictions.\n\n### B. Guardian Emergency Notification\n\nWhen Threat Mode is activated:\n\n- Notify registered guardian contacts.\n- Share the user\'s available location.\n- Display the activation time.\n- Show the current emergency status.\n\n### C. Device Damage Detection and Emergency History\n\nIf the phone becomes damaged, loses connectivity or unexpectedly stops communicating during an active Threat Mode session:\n\n- Preserve the last available emergency information.\n- Save the last known location and event timestamp.\n- Maintain the available emergency event history.\n- Notify registered guardian contacts when connectivity is available again.\n- Allow guardians to view the previously recorded emergency timeline and available evidence.\n\nThe application should distinguish between an actual device failure and a temporary network or battery issue.\n\nDo not claim that the application can detect every type of physical phone damage or continue recording after the device loses power.\n\n### D. Emergency Evidence History\n\nCreate a dedicated emergency history section containing:\n\n- Threat Mode activation time.\n- SOS activation time.\n- Available location history.\n- Recording status.\n- Emergency alert delivery status.\n- Device connectivity events.\n- Guardian notification status.\n\nOnly authorized users should be able to access this information.\n\n## 5. Additional Safety Features\n\nAdd the following features to improve user confidence and safety:\n\n### A. Trusted Guardian Network\nAllow users to register multiple trusted emergency contacts.\n\n### B. Live Location Sharing\nAllow users to share their location with authorized contacts during an emergency.\n\n### C. Emergency Status Tracking\nDisplay whether an emergency alert has been initiated, delivered or failed.\n\n### D. Fake Call Feature\nProvide an optional simulated incoming-call interface that users can activate when they need a socially convenient way to leave an uncomfortable situation.\n\n### E. Safety Check-In\nAllow users to set a check-in time. If they do not respond, notify their selected trusted contacts according to their configured preferences.\n\n### F. Emergency Offline Support\nPreserve important emergency contact information locally so it remains accessible even when internet connectivity is unavailable.\n\nClearly distinguish offline features from services that require an internet connection.\n\n### G. Privacy and Security\n- Secure user profile information.\n- Protect emergency contact details.\n- Restrict access to recordings and emergency history.\n- Provide clear consent and permission controls.\n- Allow users to manage their data and delete recordings.\n\n## 6. Overall Development Objective\n\nBuild a complete, professional, AI-powered Women Safety Application that combines intelligent voice assistance, emergency communication, dedicated safety modes, evidence management and user-friendly navigation.\n\nThe application should focus on three main objectives:\n\n1. **Prevention:** Help users identify and respond to potentially unsafe situations.\n2. **Protection:** Provide quick access to emergency assistance.\n3. **Response:** Help users communicate emergency information to trusted contacts and relevant authorities.\n\nThe final application should be intuitive, reliable, responsive and designed with user safety and privacy as its highest priorities."
    }
