  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Needs**\n\nI\'m now diving into integrating the PWA functionality, specifically focusing on utilizing `vite-plugin-pwa` for seamless installation on the phone\'s home screen. I\'m carefully dissecting each requirement to ensure comprehensive and clean integration. The goal is to establish a strong foundation for the lock-screen and home-screen shield.\n\n\n**Implementing PWA Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on the PWA\'s specifics. I\'m installing `vite-plugin-pwa` as a dev dependency and generating the required icons. I\'m setting up the configuration within `vite.config.ts`, including app details. I\'m also adding home screen shortcuts that will open the app in specific modes, such as the lock-screen shield. This will enable immediate access to key features.\n\n\n**Refining Native Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating native Android features. I\'m focusing on crafting a bridge for the lock-screen and home-screen shield with Capacitor. I\'m carefully reviewing the provided devOptions, and I\'m updating `/index.html`, `/tsconfig.json`, and the two new components (`usePWAInstall.ts` and `PWAInstallButton.tsx`). I\'m also preparing for the `/?mode=lockshield` query.\n\n\n**Integrating Native Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the native Android components. I\'m focusing on `/capacitor.config.ts`, which now points to the Vite `dist/` directory, and I\'ve configured the app ID and name. I\'ve also implemented key Kotlin services: `OurSafeBackgroundShieldService.kt`, a `ForegroundService` with critical features like shake detection, secret voice code, and SMS. I\'m also implementing  `OurSafeTapAccessibilityService.kt` for double-tap and triple-tap detection, along with `OurSafeHomeWidgetProvider.kt`, a Home Screen Widget. I\'ve also completed the Capacitor plugin (`OurSafeShieldPlugin.kt`) for bridging React and Android services for full control over the shields.\n\n\n**Enhancing UI Modes**\n\nI\'ve just finished the XML declarations, ensuring all permissions are correctly set in `/AndroidManifest.snippet.xml`, covering screen locking and system alerts. I\'m also implementing the Capacitor bridge in `/src/utils/nativeShieldBridge.ts` to sync user data and provide browser mode status. I\'ve also completed the user experience by building two modes for EmergencyLockScreenShield.tsx, that offer both lock-screen and home screen modes.\n\n\n**Defining Native Integrations**\n\nI\'m now integrating critical features. I\'m focusing on the OurSafe home screen widget, the floating shield overlay, and integrating double/triple tap detection for SOS triggering. I\'m also adding a new tab/modal inside the `QuickSosTriggersCard` that displays system mode status and lists permissions. This will enable streamlined native Android setup, and I\'ll include the necessary links.\n\n\n"
