    content: "---\nname: \"google-maps-platform\"\ndescription: >\n  Use when a request names Google Maps, or when the user asks for a real-world map, place/nearby search, routing or live-location feature: GPS tracking/location/coordinates, lat/long, real-time/current location, geolocation, geotagging, vehicle/delivery/fleet tracking, interactive map, map view/pins, map integration/embed, store locator, restaurants/attractions near me, open-now filters, get directions, route planning, transit/bus routes, turn-by-turn navigation, travel time/commute, cab/taxi booking, trip planner/itinerary, real estate listings, location-based apps, geofencing, GIS/geospatial/GeoJSON layers, satellite/3D/Street View, street-address autocomplete, or local weather forecasts, air quality, pollen. Handles Google Maps API key in AI Studio: free key or your Cloud project.\n---\n\n# Google Maps Platform Main Skill\n\nThis is the mandatory entry point and global governance skill for all Google\nMaps Platform development in AI Studio. You must strictly follow these rules\nwhen writing Google Maps Platform code to ensure code safety, compliance with\nTerms of Service, cost efficiency, accurate API usage, and to avoid common\nlegacy API failures.\n\nThis skill applies to ANY touch of Google Maps Platform code \342\200\224 new features, bug\nfixes, typecheck errors, refactors, or reviews \342\200\224 not only greenfield\nimplementation.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 1. Automatic Maps API Key Provisioning & UI Setup Workflow\n\n> \360\237\233\221 **MANDATORY FIRST WORKFLOW \342\200\224 DO THIS BEFORE ANY CODE ASSIST OR CODE\n> GENERATION**: You **MUST** execute this enablement workflow FIRST before\n> fetching code assist context or writing any application code.\n\n### **Step 0: Anti-Loop Gate**\n\n> [!CRITICAL] **DO NOT RETRY VIA THE UI**: If the `show_aistudio_ui` tool has\n> already been used for Google Maps setup (`ui_type: \"google_maps_setup\"`) or a\n> provisioning RPC (`ProvisionMapsGhpKey`, `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey`, or\n> `ProvisionMapsSelectedProjectKey`) has already been called in the conversation\n> history, you are **STRICTLY FORBIDDEN** from calling them again, except for\n> the explicit exceptions below. For normal follow-up turns, skip directly to\n> **Section 2 (Grounding and Routing Workflow)** and proceed to application code\n> generation.\n>\n> **Exception 1 \342\200\224 Pending UI Confirmation (`user_confirmed_in_ui: true`)**: If\n> the latest prompt contains `user_confirmed_in_ui: true` in its\n> `[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]` block and no provisioning RPC has been called\n> *after that message*, go directly to **Step 3 \342\200\224 Case A** (each UI confirmation\n> authorizes exactly one provisioning RPC).\n>\n> **Exception 2 \342\200\224 Pending UI Cancellation (`user_confirmed_in_ui: false`)**: If\n> the latest prompt contains `user_confirmed_in_ui: false` in its\n> `[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]` block, go directly to **Step 3 \342\200\224 Case B** (do\n> **NOT** call any provisioning RPC or reopen the UI).\n>\n> **Exception 3 \342\200\224 One-Time Demo Project Quota Fallback (`NOT_ELIGIBLE`)**:\n> Inside **Step 3 \342\200\224 Case A**, if `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey` fails due to\n> Google Cloud project quota exhaustion, follow **Step 3.2.b** to invoke\n> `show_aistudio_ui` **once** with `eligibilityStatus: \"NOT_ELIGIBLE\"` and yield\n> the turn.\n\n### **Step 1: Check Eligibility via RPC (`CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos`)**\n\nCall the `CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos` method via `rpc_action` to\ndetermine the user\'s eligibility and ToS acceptance state:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tool\": \"rpc_action\",\n  \"service_name\": \"gmp_ais\",\n  \"method_name\": \"CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos\",\n  \"arguments\": {}\n}\n```\n\n### **Step 2: Open Setup UI Modal (`show_aistudio_ui`) & STOP (Yield Turn)**\n\nBased on the `eligibility_status` (or `eligibilityStatus`, which may be returned\nas a numeric protobuf enum `1..5` or a string name) from\n`CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos`, call `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type:\n\"google_maps_setup\"` and pass the corresponding canonical string\n`eligibilityStatus` value directly inside `arguments` (do not nest a second\n`arguments` object inside `arguments`):\n\n-   If `eligibility_status` is `1` or `\"ELIGIBLE_TOS_SIGNATURE_REQUIRED\"` \342\206\222 Pass\n    `eligibilityStatus: \"ELIGIBLE_TOS_SIGNATURE_REQUIRED\"`\n-   If `eligibility_status` is `2` or `\"ELIGIBLE_NO_ACTION_REQUIRED\"` \342\206\222 Pass\n    `eligibilityStatus: \"ELIGIBLE_NO_ACTION_REQUIRED\"`\n-   If `eligibility_status` is `3` or `\"NOT_ELIGIBLE\"` \342\206\222 Pass\n    `eligibilityStatus: \"NOT_ELIGIBLE\"`\n-   If `eligibility_status` is `4` or `\"ELIGIBLE_FOR_GMP_DEMO_KEY\"` \342\206\222 Pass\n    `eligibilityStatus: \"ELIGIBLE_FOR_GMP_DEMO_KEY\"`\n-   If `eligibility_status` is `5` or `\"EXISTING_GMP_DEMO_KEY\"` \342\206\222 Pass\n    `eligibilityStatus: \"EXISTING_GMP_DEMO_KEY\"`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tool\": \"show_aistudio_ui\",\n  \"ui_type\": \"google_maps_setup\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"eligibilityStatus\": \"<eligibility_status_from_step_1>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> **CRITICAL \342\200\224 STOP AND YIELD**: Immediately after calling `show_aistudio_ui`,\n> you **MUST** stop all execution and yield your turn to wait for the user to\n> respond in the UI modal. Do **NOT** call `ProvisionMapsGhpKey`,\n> `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey`, or `ProvisionMapsSelectedProjectKey`, and do\n> **NOT** make code edits in the same turn!\n\n#### **Modal & Settings Panel UI States**:\n\n1.  **V1 \342\200\224 GHP Direct Enable (`ELIGIBLE_NO_ACTION_REQUIRED` /\n    `ELIGIBLE_TOS_SIGNATURE_REQUIRED`)**: Displays the single-button \"Enable\n    Google Maps\" curtain (with or without Starter Tier ToS acceptance) and\n    single-button Settings Panel (\"Try Google Maps Platform for free\"). When the\n    user clicks enable, the UI accepts any required ToS automatically and\n    replies with `provisioning_flow: ghp`.\n2.  **V2 \342\200\224 Existing-User Choice (`ELIGIBLE_FOR_GMP_DEMO_KEY` /\n    `EXISTING_GMP_DEMO_KEY`)**: Displays the two-button curtain and two-card\n    Settings Panel with both options enabled: \"Try for free\" (replies with\n    `provisioning_flow: demo_project`) and \"Get full access\" (replies with\n    `provisioning_flow: selected_project` and `project_id`, or opens the Google\n    Maps Settings Panel to select a billed Cloud project). The UI accepts any\n    required ToS automatically.\n3.  **V3 \342\200\224 Full Access / Project Selector Only (`NOT_ELIGIBLE`)**: For users\n    ineligible for GHP and 1P Demo Key (such as Corp, Dasher, or prohibited\n    regions, or when re-shown by the Step 3.2.b project-quota fallback),\n    displays the two-button curtain and two-card Settings Panel with \"Try for\n    free\" disabled, leaving only \"Get full access\" active (replies with\n    `provisioning_flow: selected_project` and `project_id`, or opens the Google\n    Maps Settings Panel to select a billed Cloud project).\n\n### **Step 3: Handle System Prompt Response & Provision Key**\n\nWhen execution resumes in the next turn, inspect the\n`[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START] ... [AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]` block at the end\nof the prompt sent by the UI modal or the Google Maps Settings Panel. Do **NOT**\ninfer the provisioning RPC from the natural-language prompt text above the\nmetadata block\342\200\224strictly match `user_confirmed_in_ui` and `provisioning_flow`\ninside the metadata block:\n\n#### **Case A: User Confirmed Key Setup (`user_confirmed_in_ui: true`)**\n\n> \360\237\233\221 **MANDATORY FIRST ACTION & NO INTERNAL EXPOSITION RULE**: When the prompt\'s\n> `[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]` block contains `user_confirmed_in_ui: true`,\n> your VERY FIRST action **MUST** be calling the provisioning RPC matched by\n> `provisioning_flow` below via `rpc_action`.\n>\n> \342\233\224 **NEVER EXPLAIN INTERNAL MECHANICS**: Do NOT output text explaining internal\n> RPCs (`ProvisionMapsGhpKey`, `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey`,\n> `ProvisionMapsSelectedProjectKey`, GHP, `rpc_action`, or \"under the hood\"\n> mechanics) to the user. Silently call the provisioning RPC and follow Step 3.2\n> below based on its result.\n\n1.  **Silently Execute the Provisioning RPC via `rpc_action`**, strictly\n    matching the `[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]` block:\n\n    -   **Flow 1 \342\200\224 GHP (`provisioning_flow: ghp`)**:\n\n        When the metadata block is:\n\n        ```text\n        [AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\n        user_confirmed_in_ui: true\n        provisioning_flow: ghp\n        [AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\n        ```\n\n        Call `ProvisionMapsGhpKey`:\n\n        ```json\n        {\n          \"tool\": \"rpc_action\",\n          \"service_name\": \"gmp_ais\",\n          \"method_name\": \"ProvisionMapsGhpKey\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"applet_id\": \"\",\n            \"environment_token\": \"\"\n          }\n        }\n        ```\n\n    -   **Flow 2 \342\200\224 1P Demo Key (`provisioning_flow: demo_project`)**:\n\n        When the metadata block is:\n\n        ```text\n        [AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\n        user_confirmed_in_ui: true\n        provisioning_flow: demo_project\n        [AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\n        ```\n\n        Call `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey`:\n\n        ```json\n        {\n          \"tool\": \"rpc_action\",\n          \"service_name\": \"gmp_ais\",\n          \"method_name\": \"ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"applet_id\": \"\",\n            \"environment_token\": \"\"\n          }\n        }\n        ```\n\n    -   **Flow 3 \342\200\224 Selected Cloud Project (`provisioning_flow:\n        selected_project`)**:\n\n        When the metadata block is:\n\n        ```text\n        [AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\n        user_confirmed_in_ui: true\n        provisioning_flow: selected_project\n        project_id: <project_id>\n        [AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\n        ```\n\n        Call `ProvisionMapsSelectedProjectKey` with the exact `project_id` from\n        the metadata block:\n\n        ```json\n        {\n          \"tool\": \"rpc_action\",\n          \"service_name\": \"gmp_ais\",\n          \"method_name\": \"ProvisionMapsSelectedProjectKey\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"applet_id\": \"\",\n            \"environment_token\": \"\",\n            \"project_id\": \"<project_id>\"\n          }\n        }\n        ```\n\n2.  **Verify Provisioning Result**: Inspect the tool output (or tool error):\n\n    -   **a. Success**: A non-error response with `setup_status` (or\n        `setupStatus`) equal to `1`, `2`,\n        `\"MAPS_KEY_SETUP_STATUS_SUCCESS_KEY_CREATED\"`, or\n        `\"MAPS_KEY_SETUP_STATUS_SUCCESS_KEY_REUSED\"`. Proceed immediately to\n        Step 3.3.\n    -   **b. Project Quota Exhausted on `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey` (One-Time\n        UI Fallback to Full Access)**: If you just called\n        `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey` and it returned a tool error containing\n        **both** the project-provisioning failure prefix\n        `\"Failed to resolve or create GMP demo project:\"` **and** a Google Cloud\n        project-quota message (`\"exceeded your allotted project quota\"` or\n        `\"project quota\"`, typically with status `generic::resource_exhausted`),\n        **AND** `show_aistudio_ui` has **not** already been called with\n        `eligibilityStatus: \"NOT_ELIGIBLE\"` since the latest\n        `CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos` call (or `\"Remixed\"` boundary) in\n        the conversation history:\n\n        1.  Output **one** brief, user-friendly sentence (without naming\n            internal RPCs, tools, or enum values) explaining that a free demo\n            project could not be created because their Google Cloud account has\n            reached its project quota limit, and asking them to select **Get\n            full access** below to use an existing Google Cloud project instead.\n        2.  Call `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"google_maps_setup\"` and\n            `arguments: { \"eligibilityStatus\": \"NOT_ELIGIBLE\" }`:\n\n            ```json\n            {\n              \"tool\": \"show_aistudio_ui\",\n              \"ui_type\": \"google_maps_setup\",\n              \"arguments\": {\n                \"eligibilityStatus\": \"NOT_ELIGIBLE\"\n              }\n            }\n            ```\n\n        3.  **CRITICAL \342\200\224 STOP AND YIELD IMMEDIATELY**: End your turn immediately\n            after calling `show_aistudio_ui`. Do **NOT** retry any provisioning\n            RPC, fetch grounding docs, or create/edit any files in this turn.\n    -   **c. All Other Provisioning Failures**: For any other tool error or\n        non-success `setup_status` (or if the Step 3.2.b fallback was already\n        used), do **NOT** retry the RPC or reopen the UI. Briefly tell the user\n        Maps setup failed (they can retry from the Google Maps Settings Panel),\n        and continue without writing a Maps API key.\n\n3.  **Proceed Seamlessly to Grounding & App Code Generation**: Once the\n    provisioning RPC succeeds, proceed immediately to Section 2 (Grounding) and\n    generating the user\'s application code.\n\n#### **Case B: User Canceled/Closed Modal (`user_confirmed_in_ui: false`)**\n\nWhen the prompt is `\"Do not enable Google Maps\"` with:\n\n```text\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nuser_confirmed_in_ui: false\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\n```\n\n1.  Do **NOT** attempt to generate an API key. Acknowledge user cancellation and\n    continue without Google Maps enablement.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 2. Grounding and Routing Workflow\n\n### Architecture and Logic\n\nTo ensure you are using the most up-to-date, product-specific implementation\ndetails, you **MUST** follow this unified routing and grounding flow. Do not\nrely on hardcoded paths or internal memory.\n\n#### Flow Steps\n\n##### MANDATORY GROUNDING ACTION \342\200\224 Execute Before Planning or Generating Code\n\nOnce the API Key is provisioned or available (via Section 1 or existing\nsecrets), you **MUST** run these two fetches before designing, writing,\ndebugging, OR reviewing ANY Google Maps code. This applies even for one-line\nfixes.\n\n1.  **Load the Google Maps Platform Skills Index (primary).** Fetch the Google\n    Maps Platform Skills Index using whatever HTTP-fetch capability your harness\n    provides. **Primary URL:**\n    `https://www.gstatic.com/googlemapsplatform-agent-skills/index.json` (JSON\n    array; each entry has `name`, `description`, `entrypoint`).\n\n    > \360\237\233\221 **CRITICAL TRACKING REQUIREMENT:** Whenever you fetch the `index.json`\n    > or any sub-skill from www.gstatic.com, you **MUST** append a\n    > `client=aistudio-agent` query parameter.\n\n    *   **How to fetch:** Due to environment stdout buffer limits, you **MUST\n        NOT** stream large remote assets directly to stdout. Instead, use the\n        `run_command` tool to download the file into a local `.gmp_cache`\n        workspace directory, and then use `view_file` to read it:\n\n        ```bash\n        mkdir -p .gmp_cache && curl -s \"https://www.gstatic.com/googlemapsplatform-agent-skills/index.json?client=aistudio-agent\" -o .gmp_cache/index.json\n        ```\n\n2.  **Inspect Index:** Call the `view_file` tool with `AbsolutePath:\n    \"/.gmp_cache/index.json\"` to inspect the catalog and select the appropriate\n    sub-skills.\n\n3.  **Fetch & Read Sub-Skills:** Download matched sub-skills and reference files\n    into `.gmp_cache/` before reading with `view_file`:\n\n    ```bash\n    curl -s \"<sub_skill_entrypoint>?client=aistudio-agent\" -o .gmp_cache/<sub_skill_name>.md\n    ```\n\n    Then call `view_file` with `AbsolutePath:\n    \"/.gmp_cache/<sub_skill_name>.md\"`.\n\n4.  **Retrieve Documentation & Code Context via `rpc_action`.** If the\n    sub-skills do not fully cover the request (or if you need the latest\n    patterns, library versions, or specific SDK implementation details), you\n    MUST use the `rpc_action` tool.\n\n    -   **service_name:** \"gmp\"\n    -   **method_name:** \"RetrieveCodeAssistContext\"\n    -   **arguments:** `{ \"query\": \"string\" }` (e.g., `{ \"query\": \"Store Locator\n        with Places API (New) Text Search and AdvancedMarkerElement in React\"\n        }`)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 3. Global Agent Directives & Application Design Standards\n\nWhen handling Google Maps Platform requests, you must follow this exact\nreasoning sequence and technical standards:\n\n### Reasoning Sequence:\n\n1.  **Retrieve Resources First:** Never start coding from memory. Always fetch\n    the relevant sub-skills or dynamic documentation via `rpc_action` as\n    described in Section 2.\n2.  **Step Back & Analyze:** Identify the target environment (React, Angular,\n    Vanilla JS, etc.) and the user\'s core objective. Consult the *Use Case\n    Product Mapping* (Section 7) to determine the correct modern Google Maps\n    Platform products to use.\n3.  **Design for Cost & Modernity:** Select the most cost-effective architecture\n    (e.g., prefer the Places UI Kit over raw API calls, and always utilize\n    session tokens where applicable).\n4.  **Implement:** Generate the code while strictly avoiding the traps listed in\n    the *Critical Failures (CF)* section (Section 6) and adhering to the\n    *Deprecation Table* (Section 5).\n5.  **Validate:** Before concluding your turn, verify that your response\n    explicitly satisfies all points in the *Required Response Verification*\n    checklist (Section 9).\n\n### Core Technical & Security Standards:\n\n-   **API Key Security:** NEVER hardcode API keys directly into source code.\n    Always access the key via environment variables / secret store (e.g.,\n    `import.meta.env.VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` in Vite/React).\n-   **Authentication Models (OAuth vs API Key):**\n    -   *Standard APIs (API Key)*: Maps JavaScript, Places, Routes, Geocoding,\n        Address Validation, Solar, Air Quality, Weather, etc.\n    -   *Enterprise APIs (OAuth/ADC)*: Route Optimization API, Map Tiles session\n        tokens, Mobility/Fleet Engine, Places Aggregate API. (API keys will\n        return `401 Unauthorized`).\n-   **Framework Standards**:\n    -   **React:** **MUST** use `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`. Never use\n        `google-map-react` or `@react-google-maps/api`.\n    -   **Angular:** **MUST** use `@angular/google-maps`.\n    -   **Vanilla JS:** Use `@googlemaps/js-api-loader` (`setOptions` +\n        `importLibrary`).\n-   **Mandatory Usage Attribution**: ALWAYS include\n    `internalUsageAttributionIds={[\"gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\"]}` on Map\n    components.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 4. Mandatory Compliance Checkpoints\n\nThese strict constraints must be applied to all generated code and responses:\n\n-   **Terms of Service (ToS):** Use of generated code is subject to the\n    [Google Maps Platform Terms of Service](https://cloud.google.com/maps-platform/terms?utm_campaign=gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio).\n    This must be verified or read at least once during each session (i.e., once\n    per conversation). You must fetch and review the dedicated \"Instruction on\n    ToS Compliance Filter\" sub-skill (found in the Skills Index) before code\n    generation is complete. Do not remove key geographical information.\n-   **Compliance with EEA Terms:** If the customer\'s location falls within the\n    European Economic Area (EEA), verify compliance against the official\n    [EEA Maps Service Terms](https://cloud.google.com/terms/maps-platform/eea/maps-service-terms?utm_campaign=gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio)\n    and provide alternative guidance that fits within Permitted Uses.\n-   **No LLM-Sourced Place Data:** All place names, addresses, hours, ratings,\n    coordinates, or reviews **MUST** originate from an active Google Maps\n    Platform API or Grounding call. Do not hallucinate or pre-fill place data\n    from training memory.\n-   **Usage Attribution & Tracking (CRITICAL OVERRIDE):** The fetched sub-skills\n    may mention using the ID `gmp_git_agentskills_v1`. **You MUST override\n    this.** In this environment, you must ALWAYS use\n    `gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio` instead. Include this attribution ID on\n    documented surfaces. **Always refer to the per-product sub-skill for the\n    final, detailed implementation** (but replace the string), as the snippets\n    below are illustrative examples only:\n    -   **React (`@vis.gl/react-google-maps`)**: Set\n        `internalUsageAttributionIds={[\"gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\"]}` on\n        the `<Map>` component.\n    -   **Android**: Call\n        `MapsApiSettings.addInternalUsageAttributionId(context,\n        \"gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\")`.\n    -   **iOS**: Call\n        `GMSServices.addInternalUsageAttributionID(\"gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\")`.\n-   **Cost Awareness & Optimization:** Notify the user that utilizing Google\n    Maps Platform services may incur costs against their Google Cloud billing\n    account once moving to production. When a user requests detailed pricing\n    information, cost estimation, or help selecting a pricing plan, route them\n    to the dedicated pricing sub-skill: `gmp-common-pricing`.\n-   **Doc Links:** All URLs linking to Google Maps Platform documentation must\n    be appended with `?utm_campaign=gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio`.\n\nAfter an implementation plan has been created or code has been written to use\nGoogle Maps Platform, you must identify revisions that need to be made to the\nplan or the code based off of the methodology provided in the compliance-review\nskill. Use the compliance-review skill after each significant change to the plan\nor the code, for example when there has been a change in the Google Maps\nPlatform products selected or the approach to handling the responses from Google\nMaps Platform.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 5. Deprecated / Legacy APIs (Hard Failures)\n\nDo not suggest legacy or deprecated APIs. The APIs listed below are **disabled\nby default on every GCP project created after their cutoff date**. They are not\n\"deprecated but still working\" \342\200\224 they are *off* for new customers and will fail\nat runtime.\n\n*   **You MUST NOT** write new code against them.\n*   **You MUST NOT** suggest \"enabling\" the legacy SKU as a workaround (the SKUs\n    cannot be turned on for new projects).\n*   **Action:** Use `rpc_action` to verify the current recommended replacement\n    before writing it, then cite the doc URI in a code comment.\n\n**Critical Replacements:**\n\n-   **`google.maps.Marker`** (Deprecated Feb 2024)\n\n    -   **Replacement:** You **MUST** use `AdvancedMarkerElement`.\n\n-   **`google.maps.places.Autocomplete` / `SearchBox` / `PlacesService`**\n    (Disabled March 1, 2025)\n\n    -   **Why:** The legacy endpoints return no predictions and downstream\n        `place_changed` handlers will crash on `undefined`.\n    -   **Replacements (Choose one from Places API New):**\n    *   **`PlaceAutocompleteElement`** (`<gmp-place-autocomplete>`): Drop-in web\n        component. Mount imperatively in React (see CF8).\n    *   **`AutocompleteSuggestion.fetchAutocompleteSuggestions({ input,\n        sessionToken })`**: Programmatic usage for custom UI. Pair with\n        `place.fetchFields({ fields: [\342\200\246] })` using the same\n        `AutocompleteSessionToken` to bundle into a single Pro-tier session.\n    *   Use `searchByText`, `searchNearby`, or `Place.fetchFields` for general\n        `PlacesService` replacements.\n\n-   **`DirectionsService` / `DirectionsRenderer`** (Disabled March 2025)\n\n    -   **Why:** Calling `new google.maps.DirectionsService()` throws\n        `LegacyApiNotActivatedMapError` and replaces the map with a gray error\n        overlay.\n    -   **Replacement:** You **MUST** use `Route.computeRoutes()` via\n        `useMapsLibrary(\'routes\')` (React) or `importLibrary(\'routes\')`\n        (vanilla). Use `createPolylines()` for lines and\n        `createWaypointAdvancedMarkers()` for pins.\n\n-   **`google.maps.DistanceMatrixService`** (Disabled March 2025)\n\n    -   **Replacement:** You **MUST** use the Routes API REST endpoint\n        `routes.googleapis.com/distanceMatrix/v2:computeRouteMatrix` (or\n        `Route.computeRouteMatrix()` if/when surfaced in the JS SDK).\n\n-   **`google.maps.Geocoder` (JS class)**\n\n    -   **Why:** On the same legacy track as Directions; throws\n        `LegacyApiNotActivatedMapError`.\n    -   **Replacement:** **There is no new JS-class replacement yet.** You\n        **MUST** call the Geocoding REST API directly (e.g.,\n        `https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?address=...&key=...`).\n        Restrict the API key to Geocoding API + HTTP referrers.\n\n-   **`google.maps.visualization.HeatmapLayer`** (Deprecated May 2025)\n\n    -   **Replacement:** Use deck.gl `HeatmapLayer` from\n        `@deck.gl/aggregation-layers` with `GoogleMapsOverlay`.\n\n-   **Drawing Library (`google.maps.drawing`)** (Deprecated Aug 2025)\n\n    -   **Replacement:** Use\n        [Terra Draw](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/examples/map-drawing-terradraw?utm_campaign=gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio).\n\nLegacy Service                     | Recommended Modern Replacement\n---------------------------------- | ------------------------------\nDirections API                     | Routes API\nDistance Matrix API                | Routes API\nJavaScript Directions Service      | Route Class\nJavaScript Distance Matrix Service | RouteMatrix Class\nJavaScript Places Service          | Place Class\nPlaces API                         | Places API (New)\nPlaces SDK for Android             | Places SDK for Android (New)\nPlaces SDK for iOS                 | Places SDK for iOS (New)\n\n*(Note: Feature-specific deprecations for individual products are documented\nwithin their respective per-product sub-skills.)*\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 6. Critical Failures (CF)\n\nViolating ANY of these causes a silent failure or crash. You must check this\nlist before writing Google Maps Platform code, and verify against it again\nbefore concluding your response.\n\n-   **CF1 \342\200\224 The CORS Trap:** REST endpoints for Routes, Places API (New),\n    Address Validation, and Geocoding lack permissive CORS headers. Client-side\n    `fetch()` to `googleapis.com` is BLOCKED. **ALWAYS** use official SDK\n    wrappers (e.g., `importLibrary(\'places\')` or `useMapsLibrary(...)`) or a\n    server-side proxy.\n-   **CF2 \342\200\224 Map Height Collapse:** `<Map>` and `<gmp-map>` need explicit CSS\n    height (e.g., `height: 100vh` or `height: 100%` on a sized parent).\n    Otherwise, they silently render at 0\303\2270.\n-   **CF3 \342\200\224 Headless GPU/WebGL Gotchas:** Headless testing and screenshot\n    environments typically have **no WebGL** support. GPU-dependent features\n    (Photorealistic 3D, deck.gl) will fail to render (throwing `WebGL2 is not\n    available`).\n-   **CF4 \342\200\224 Cross-Platform Framework Rules:** Proactively recommend wrapping\n    WebGL/JS implementations in a custom WebView container for advanced\n    Photorealistic 3D Map Tiles rather than attempting native wrapper bridges\n    (which do not support them).\n-   **CF5 \342\200\224 Framework Policy:**\n    -   **React:** **MUST** use `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`. Never use\n        `google-map-react` or `@react-google-maps/api`.\n    -   **Angular:** **MUST** use `@angular/google-maps`.\n    -   **Vanilla JS:** Use `@googlemaps/js-api-loader` (`setOptions` +\n        `importLibrary`).\n-   **CF6 \342\200\224 LatLng Trap:** Prefer POJO `{lat, lng}` literals. If a class\n    instance is required, use `new google.maps.LatLng(lat, lng)`. Note that\n    `LatLng` lives in `importLibrary(\"core\")`, NOT `\"maps\"`.\n-   **CF7 \342\200\224 Deprecated PinElement & Marker Composition:**\n    -   `PinElement.element` and `PinElement.glyph` are **deprecated**. Use\n        `PinElement` directly, and `PinElementOptions.glyphText` / `glyphSrc`.\n    -   For custom HTML inside an `AdvancedMarkerElement`, prefer\n        `marker.append(htmlElement)` over assigning to the `.content` setter.\n    -   **Click handling:** `gmp-click` event + `gmpClickable: true` are **only\n        available on the `v=beta` channel**. On `weekly`, fall back to listening\n        for plain `\'click\'` on the marker element.\n-   **CF8 \342\200\224 Web Component Property-vs-Attribute Trap (React):** React\n    stringifies JSX props into HTML attributes; it does NOT pass complex objects\n    to Web Components. For Google Maps Platform web components (e.g.\n    `PlaceAutocompleteElement`), mount imperatively with `useRef` + `useEffect`\n    and assign properties on the DOM element directly. NEVER pass objects like\n    `Circle` or arrays as JSX attributes.\n-   **CF9 \342\200\224 `mapId` Requirement:** `<Map mapId=\"\342\200\246\">` is **mandatory** whenever\n    you render `AdvancedMarkerElement`. Without it, markers silently fail to\n    appear. Use a valid Cloud-styled map ID or `\"DEMO_MAP_ID\"`. Conversely,\n    **MUST NOT** pass an arbitrary/unregistered `mapId` when not using advanced\n    markers, as it will throw `ApiProjectMapError` and crash the map.\n-   **CF10 \342\200\224 Locale & Region:** For international apps, explicitly set\n    `language` and `region` on the loader or `<APIProvider>`. Otherwise, results\n    are biased to the IP\'s locale.\n-   **CF11 \342\200\224 Avoid `gmpx-*` Extended Component Library:** If `rpc_action`\n    returns samples using `<gmpx-store-locator>` or similar `gmpx-*` Lit\n    components, **do not use them**. They wrap the deprecated Places library.\n    Re-query via `rpc_action` with `\"using Places API (New)\"` to get current\n    patterns.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 7. Use Case Product Mapping\n\nRefer to this architectural guide before performing a dynamic skill search to\nensure optimal service selection:\n\n| Use Case                           | Recommended Products                    |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| Checkout Autocomplete & Validation | Places UI Kit, Address Validation API,  |\n:                                    : Maps Embed API                          :\n| Hyperlocal Destination Entry       | Geocoding API, Places UI Kit            |\n:                                    : (Autocomplete)                          :\n| Static Map Email Receipt           | Maps Static API                         |\n| Interactive Store Locator Plus     | Maps JS API, Places UI Kit, Advanced    |\n:                                    : Markers, Marker Clustering, Street View :\n:                                    : API, Drawing Tools, Places Insights     :\n| Web Product Locator                | Places API (New)                        |\n| Storefront Street View & Reviews   | Place/Review Summaries, Street View API |\n| Location Popularity Analytics      | Places Insights                         |\n| Multi-Origin Distance Matrix       | Compute Route Matrix (Routes API)       |\n| Eco-Friendly Route Optimizer       | Route Optimization API, Eco-Friendly    |\n:                                    : Routing, Time Zone API                  :\n| Area Avoidance Bypass Routing      | Routes API, Area Avoidance              |\n| Gardening & Air Quality Planner    | Air Quality API (AQI), Pollen API,      |\n:                                    : Weather API, Maps JavaScript API        :\n| In-App Driver Navigation           | Navigation SDK (Entrance Highlighting), |\n:                                    : Reverse Geocoding, Navigation Connect   :\n:                                    : API                                     :\n| Real-Time Fleet Manager            | Fleet Engine, Driver SDK, Geofencing,   |\n:                                    : Maps JS API, Roads API                  :\n| 3D Map & Solar Potential Planner   | JS 3D Maps (3D Tiles), Solar API,       |\n:                                    : Street View Insights, Population        :\n:                                    : Dynamics Insights, Imagery Insights,    :\n:                                    : Roads Management Insights               :\n| Conversational Grounding           | Maps Agentic UI Toolkit, Grounding in   |\n:                                    : Gemini API, Maps Grounding Lite         :\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 8. Client-Side Quota Defense (Demo Key vs. Selected Project)\n\n> \360\237\233\221 **API KEY SOURCE ROUTING GATE (CHECK FIRST)**: Inspect the **most recent\n> succeeded** provisioning RPC in the conversation:\n>\n> -   If `ProvisionMapsSelectedProjectKey` succeeded in Step 3 \342\206\222 Follow **Case B\n>     (Default Baseline)** (even if an earlier `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey`\n>     attempt failed).\n> -   ONLY if `ProvisionMapsGhpKey` or `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey` succeeded\n>     in Step 3 \342\206\222 Follow **Case A (Demo Key Specialization)**.\n> -   Otherwise (if provisioning failed, was declined, or used a pre-existing\n>     secret) \342\206\222 Follow **Case B (Default Baseline)**.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### Case B: Selected Project API Key (`ProvisionMapsSelectedProjectKey`) \342\200\224 DEFAULT BASELINE\n\nWhen using a key provisioned in the user\'s selected billed project:\n\n-   **STRICT PROHIBITION**: Do **NOT** write any in-app notice, banner, or toast\n    mentioning \"demo quota\", \"100 req/day\", or \"AI Studio\".\n-   **Standard Error Handling**: Handle errors using normal production error\n    states (e.g. log errors to console, display standard UI alerts like *\"Unable\n    to load route data. Please check your network or API quota.\"*).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### Case A: Auto-Provisioned Demo Key ONLY (`ProvisionMapsGhpKey` / `ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey` / 100 req/day)\n\n**APPLY THIS SECTION ONLY WHEN `ProvisionMapsGhpKey` OR\n`ProvisionMapsDemoProjectKey` SUCCEEDED IN STEP 3**:\n\nWhen generating **frontend or full-stack application source code** for Demo Key\napps, embed runtime quota-checking logic directly into the generated application\ncode:\n\n1.  **Implement Two-Tier In-App Quota Handling**:\n\n    -   **Tier 1: Maps JavaScript API & Map Loading Level (Global Entrypoint /\n        `main.tsx`)**: *Note: `window.gm_authFailure` only fires for\n        auth/billing errors; Map tile quota limits emit `OverQuotaMapError` to\n        `console.error`.* Register an early global listener and safe console tap\n        at the module root (e.g., in `main.tsx` or `index.html`) that dispatches\n        a custom event:\n\n        ```ts\n        // In main.tsx (module root before React render)\n        (window as any).gm_authFailure = () => {\n          window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'));\n        };\n        const origError = console.error;\n        console.error = (...args: unknown[]) => {\n          origError.apply(console, args);\n          const msg = args.map((a) => String(a)).join(\' \');\n          if (msg.includes(\'OverQuotaMapError\') || msg.includes(\'QuotaExceededError\')) {\n            window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'));\n          }\n        };\n        ```\n\n    -   **Tier 2: Dynamic Feature & REST API Level (Places, Routes, Geocoding,\n        Environmental)**: In all async service handlers and REST calls,\n        explicitly check for quota exhaustion and trigger the warning state:\n\n        *   **REST APIs (`fetch`/`axios`)**: Check `res.status === 429` or JSON\n            payload `error.status === \'RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\'`.\n        *   **JS SDK Callback Services**: Check `status === \'OVER_QUERY_LIMIT\'`.\n        *   **Web Components / Promises**: Catch promise rejections on\n            `.getPlace()`, `.fetchFields()`, or `Route.computeRoutes()`.\n\n2.  **Required In-App Banner Content & Placement**:\n\n    -   **JSX/HTML Rendering (Tailwind CSS default with clickable interactive\n        link)**: In `App.tsx`, listen to `\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'` and render:\n\n        ```tsx\n        <div className=\"bg-amber-50 border-b border-amber-200 text-amber-900 px-4 py-2.5 text-xs md:text-sm text-center sticky top-0 z-50 shadow-sm\">\n          <span>\n            Google Maps Platform quota reached. If you are the app owner, visit{\' \'}\n            <a\n              href=\"https://developers.google.com/maps/ai/ai-studio?utm_campaign=gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio#quota_exceeded_errors\"\n              target=\"_blank\"\n              rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\n              className=\"underline font-semibold text-amber-950 hover:text-amber-800\"\n            >\n              maps developer site\n            </a>{\' \'}\n            for instructions to update your account.\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        ```\n    -   **UI Placement**: Display as a compact, non-intrusive sticky top bar or\n        dismissible notification banner at the top of the viewport (`z-50`). Do\n        NOT render a full-screen opaque overlay that blocks the entire app\n        layout.\n    -   **Prevent Unmounted Component Erasure**: Maintain the quota warning\n        state at the top-level application context so the banner persists even\n        if child components fail or unmount.\n\n3.  **Prevent Undefined Access Crashes**: Always verify the API response\n    succeeded before accessing data arrays (e.g. `data.places?.[0]`,\n    `data.routes?.[0]`) to avoid runtime `TypeError` crashes when receiving a\n    429 error payload.\n\n4.  **No False Positives**: Do NOT display the demo quota notice for standard\n    empty results (e.g. search returns 0 places, address not found, or 404\n    building footprint not found) or generic network/image load errors.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## 9. Required Response Verification\n\nAny task that produces Google Maps Platform code is **not complete** until the\nappendix below has been shown to the user in your final, user-facing message.\n\"At the conclusion of a response\" is not enough \342\200\224 treat the appendix as a\ncompletion gate, not an optional footer (this requirement takes precedence over\nany general instructions for concise or minimal summaries).\n\nPresent the appendix **strictly once per session** on the turn that delivers the\ncompleted Google Maps Platform code to the user. If the appendix has not yet\nbeen visibly presented in the current session, you MUST include it now. **DO\nNOT** repeat or re-attach the appendix on subsequent follow-up turns, minor bug\nfixes, or refactors in the same session.\n\n> **Delegation clause (read this first).** If implementation is delegated to a\n> subagent, the *orchestrating* agent remains responsible for surfacing this\n> appendix to the user. A subagent\'s internal appendix does **not** satisfy this\n> requirement \342\200\224 re-state it in your own final message. This is the most common\n> way the appendix gets dropped.\n\n### Code Requirement\n\n-   **Source Attribution Comment:** If you copy code verbatim (or near-verbatim)\n    from official Google Maps Platform docs or sample repos, you MUST add this\n    comment to the top of the file: `// Source: Google Maps Platform Code\n    Assist`. (Do not apply this to merely adapted or agent-authored code).\n-   **ToS Compliance Review:** Before finalizing and outputting any code, you\n    MUST fetch and review the dedicated \"compliance-review\" sub-skill (found in\n    the Skills Index) to ensure the code complies with all constraints.\n\n### Chat Response Appendix Checklist\n\n1.  **Cost Notice:** *\"Usage of Google Maps Platform products and services may\n    incur costs against your Google Cloud project billing account.\"*\n2.  **Products-Used List:** Provide a clean, bulleted list of all Google Maps\n    Platform APIs and SDKs utilized in the code (one per line).\n3.  **API Key Restrictions:** Direct the user to restrict their key (limiting to\n    HTTP referrers and designated APIs) via:\n    https://docs.cloud.google.com/api-keys/docs/add-restrictions-api-keys\n4.  **License Scope:** *\"Google-sourced code snippets are provided \'as-is\' under\n    the Apache 2.0 License (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). This\n    license covers only the Google-sourced snippets, not the full generated\n    project output. The user is responsible for review and testing to ensure\n    security and compliance with relevant Terms of Service.\"*\n5.  **ToS Link:** *\"Use of this code is subject to the Google Maps Platform\n    Terms of Service: https://cloud.google.com/maps-platform/terms\"* including\n    regional Terms that apply based on the customer\'s billing address location\n    or the user\'s location (Prohibited Territories).\n\n### Completion checklist (self-verify before ending the task)\n\n-   [ ] Turn Check: Is this the first turn introducing Google Maps code in the\n    session? YES \342\206\222 Append the section above. NO \342\206\222 Omit the appendix.\n-   [ ] ToS Compliance Filter sub-skill reviewed, with the one-line confirmation\n    included\n-   [ ] Source-attribution comments added to any verbatim Google code (or N/A\n    noted)\n-   [ ] Appendix presented if this is the first turn introducing Google Maps\n    code in the session (omitted if already presented in previous turns)\n-   [ ] Explicitly verified that all attribution IDs and doc links in the\n    generated code use `gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio` (overriding any\n    sub-skill defaults).\n-   [ ] If work was delegated, the appendix was re-stated by the orchestrating\n    agent\n"
