    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\nThe user is finalizing **OurSafe**, an AI-powered Women Safety Application (React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + Express + Gemini Live/Hydrogen + VitePWA + Capacitor Android native package), before connecting their own backend.\n\nIn the **latest comprehensive final-feature request**, the user asked for ALL of the following to be automated, verified, and production-clean:\n1. **Threat Mode (\"dread mode\") Automatic Continuous Audio & Video Recording**:\n   - The moment Threat Mode activates, **automatically start continuous video+audio recording** (falling back seamlessly to continuous audio-only if camera is unavailable) with **no extra manual confirmation modal/clicks** \342\200\224 continuously recording for safety until the user taps \"I\'m Safe \342\200\224 Deactivate\" or stops it, and auto-saving chunks/recording to IndexedDB Evidence History.\n2. **Travel Mode \342\200\224 Real Google Maps Two-Location Route Tracking + Live Off-Route Deviation Alert**:\n   - Maintain clear, accurate **Start \342\206\222 Destination** route plotting on **real Google Maps** (`@vis.gl/react-google-maps` + modern **Routes API** `Route.computeRoutes()`, NO legacy `DirectionsService`/`Marker`).\n   - Continuously monitor live GPS movement during Travel Mode (`navigator.geolocation.watchPosition` + optional live off-route simulation test button for desktop testing) and **automatically alert the mobile user (audible alarm + urgent visual alert + automatic guardian alert option + quick SOS escalation)** if the vehicle moves away from the Google Maps route corridor (e.g., > 150m\342\200\223250m off the planned route polyline).\n3. **Travel Mode \342\200\224 Vehicle / Auto Number Verification + Photo Capture (\"verify auto number / photo income\")**:\n   - Add a **Vehicle / Auto Number Verification & Photo Capture** section in Travel Mode:\n     - Enter auto/cab/bike registration number (e.g., `TN 09 AB 1234`) OR capture/upload a photo of the vehicle/plate (with AI OCR reading the plate via Gemini server endpoint `/api/travel/verify-vehicle`!).\n     - Validate registration format (Indian RTO state/district/series pattern & general plate validation + checksum/format audit), transparently check format authenticity and flag suspicious/fake/invalid plate patterns honestly (clearly indicating backend RTO/Vahan API hookup point without inventing fake owner names), save the vehicle number + timestamped photo into the active `TravelSession` & `EmergencyHistory`, and attach the verified vehicle number to guardian SMS/SOS alerts!\n4. **Automated SOS Process (\"Red Rose\" secret code / Lock Shield \342\200\224 Automatic Call + Automatic Message Dispatch)**:\n   - When the user triggers SOS via the **\"Red Rose\"** secret voice code (or 3x Shake / Double or Triple Tap / Lock Shield), make the SOS flow **fully automated**:\n     - Default `quickTriggerCountdownSec: 0` (or immediate automated dispatch option) + automatic emergency call (`tel:` + native `ACTION_CALL` in Android bridge) AND **automatic emergency alert/message dispatch** (server-side `/api/sos/dispatch` webhook-ready endpoint logging & returning real dispatch status + automatic Guardian SMS/WhatsApp/direct `sms:` payload + Police dispatch) + **Share live location to BOTH Guardian AND Police**!\n5. **AI Voice Controller \342\200\224 Full Hands-Free App-Wide Voice Control (\"total app based on voice input, not manual input\")**:\n   - When AI Voice is ON, keep it active **across the entire app** (lift Live Voice / continuous Voice Controller bar to `HomeDashboard` level or persistent floating voice controller pill so navigating to SOS, Threat, Travel, Nearby, History does **NOT** kill the voice session!).\n   - Saying `\"Go to SOS\"` / `\"Open SOS\"` automatically navigates to SOS & activates emergency call + message dispatch; `\"Activate Threat Mode\"` navigates to Threat Mode & auto-starts continuous audio+video recording + AI nearby police lookup; `\"Share my location\"` / `\"Share my business\"` shares live location with **BOTH Guardian AND Police**; `\"Find nearby police\"` / `\"Police numbers\"` runs AI police lookup immediately; `\"Open Travel Mode\"` navigates to Travel Mode.\n6. **AI Nearby Police Station Numbers**:\n   - Ensure `/api/threat/nearby-police` continues returning clean, reliable nearby police stations & contact numbers (already fixed with 3-tier waterfall: Gemini Maps Grounding \342\206\222 Gemini Google Search Grounding \342\206\222 OpenStreetMap Nominatim).\n7. **Final Verification of Everything**:\n   - Verify all buttons, HTML/CSS styling (OurSafe botanical sage theme: `#CDD7C1` canvas, `#FCFDF9` cards, `#2F4526` deep olive accent), Google Maps route + deviation alerts, vehicle verification, auto-recording, voice control, and zero TypeScript/lint/runtime errors.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n\n#### Completed Prior to Current Turn (Verified & Running)\n- **3 Hands-Free & Outside-App Emergency SOS Triggers** (`useEmergencyQuickTriggers.ts`, `EmergencyTriggerOverlay.tsx`, `EmergencyLockScreenShield.tsx`, `QuickSosTriggersCard.tsx`, `SettingsModal.tsx`, `SosPage.tsx`, `LoginScreen.tsx`, `App.tsx`, `HomeDashboard.tsx`):\n  - 3x Phone Shake (`DeviceMotionEvent`), Always-On Secret Voice Code (`SpeechRecognition`, default `\"Red Rose\"`), Double/Triple Screen Tap (`pointerdown`), Lock-Screen + Home-Screen Standby Shield, and pre-login SOS access.\n- **PWA Home Screen Installability** (`vite.config.ts` with `vite-plugin-pwa`, `public/icon.svg`, `public/pwa-192x192.png`, `public/pwa-512x512.png`, `public/pwa-maskable-512x512.png`, `public/apple-touch-icon.png`, `src/hooks/usePWAInstall.ts`, `src/components/PWAInstallButton.tsx`, `index.html`, `tsconfig.json`).\n- **Native Android Lock-Screen & Home-Screen Package** (`capacitor.config.ts`, `src/utils/nativeShieldBridge.ts`, `android-native/OurSafeBackgroundShieldService.kt`, `OurSafeTapAccessibilityService.kt`, `OurSafeHomeWidgetProvider.kt`, `OurSafeShieldPlugin.kt`, `AndroidManifest.snippet.xml`).\n- **Threat Mode AI Police Lookup 429 Fix** (`server.ts` 3-tier waterfall verified returning HTTP 200 for `Chennai`).\n\n#### Completed in Current Turn (Google Maps Provisioning \342\200\224 DO NOT REPEAT!)\n1. **Read Skills**:\n   - `/skills/system_skills/google_maps_platform/SKILL.md` (read completely).\n   - `/skills/system_skills/pwa_integration/SKILL.md` (read earlier).\n2. **Provisioned Google Maps API Key via GHP (`ProvisionMapsGhpKey`)**:\n   - Called `CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos` \342\206\222 returned `eligibility_status: 1`.\n   - Called `show_aistudio_ui` (`google_maps_setup`) \342\206\222 user confirmed (`user_confirmed_in_ui: true`, `provisioning_flow: ghp`).\n   - Called `ProvisionMapsGhpKey` via `rpc_action` \342\206\222 **SUCCEEDED (`setup_status: 1`, \"Maps API Key successfully provisioned.\")**.\n   - **CRITICAL ANTI-LOOP GATE**: Do **NOT** call `show_aistudio_ui` (`google_maps_setup`) or any Maps provisioning RPC again!\n   - **CRITICAL CASE A RULE**: Because `ProvisionMapsGhpKey` succeeded, **Section 8 Case A (Demo Key Quota Defense)** applies \342\200\224 we MUST add the `gm_authFailure` / `OverQuotaMapError` listener in `src/main.tsx` and the non-intrusive sticky quota banner in `src/App.tsx`!\n3. **Started Google Maps Grounding**:\n   - Downloaded `https://www.gstatic.com/googlemapsplatform-agent-skills/index.json?client=aistudio-agent` to `/.gmp_cache/index.json`.\n   - **NOT YET READ**: Must view `/.gmp_cache/index.json`, then fetch & read the matched sub-skills (specifically **ToS compliance-review**, **Maps JS / React `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`**, and **Routes API `Route.computeRoutes()`**) into `/.gmp_cache/` before writing Google Maps code!\n4. **Inspected Existing App Files**:\n   - Viewed `/server.ts`, `/.env.example`, `/src/components/pages/ThreatModePage.tsx`, `/src/components/pages/TravelModePage.tsx`, `/src/components/dashboard/TravelModePanel.tsx`, `/src/components/pages/AiVoiceAssistantPage.tsx`.\n   - **No code changes made yet for the latest user request.**\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Google Maps API Key Environment Variable**: After `ProvisionMapsGhpKey`, check `.env` / `.env.local` or `process.env` (note `env | grep -iE \'MAPS|GOOGLE\'` in the shell didn\'t print `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` yet \342\200\224 check if `.env` or `.env.local` was written by `ProvisionMapsGhpKey` or if the dev server needs restart / `vite.config.ts` exposes `process.env.GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` or `import.meta.env.VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY`!). Inspect workspace root with `list_dir` or check `.env*` safely (without printing secret values) before wiring `apiKey`.\n- **Google Maps Strict Requirements (from `google_maps_platform/SKILL.md`)**:\n  - React **MUST** use `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` (install via `install_applet_package`).\n  - **NEVER** use deprecated `google.maps.Marker`, `DirectionsService`/`DirectionsRenderer`, `google.maps.Geocoder` JS class, or legacy `PlacesService`/`Autocomplete`.\n  - **MUST** use `AdvancedMarkerElement` (with `mapId=\"DEMO_MAP_ID\"`), `Route.computeRoutes()` via `useMapsLibrary(\'routes\')` (or server proxy to Routes API v2 + Geocoding REST API), and `internalUsageAttributionIds={[\"gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\"]}` on `<Map>`!\n  - **MUST** fetch & read `/.gmp_cache/index.json` + relevant sub-skills (including **compliance-review / ToS Compliance Filter**) via `curl ...?client=aistudio-agent` before writing Maps code.\n  - **MUST** append the **Required Response Verification Appendix** (Section 9 of `google_maps_platform/SKILL.md`) once at the end of the final response introducing Google Maps code!\n- **Current AI Voice Architecture**: Currently `AiVoiceAssistantPage` owns the WebSocket `/api/live-voice` connection, so when a voice command calls `setActivePage(\'sos\')` or `setActivePage(\'threat\')`, `AiVoiceAssistantPage` unmounts and drops the live voice connection! Lifting the global voice session controller (or keeping a persistent Voice Controller hook/bar mounted in `HomeDashboard.tsx`) fixes this completely so the user can navigate the ENTIRE app hands-free by voice!\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Resolved earlier**:\n  - `TypeError: onFetchNearbyPoliceAi is not a function` in `ThreatModePage.tsx` \342\206\222 fixed by wiring props in `HomeDashboard.tsx`.\n  - `429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` from Gemini Maps Grounding on `/api/threat/nearby-police` \342\206\222 fixed in `/server.ts` with 3-tier waterfall (Maps Grounding \342\206\222 Search Grounding \342\206\222 OpenStreetMap Nominatim), verified returning HTTP 200.\n  - External `@capacitor/cli` type import in `capacitor.config.ts` \342\206\222 removed import so `tsc --noEmit` stays clean.\n- **No unresolved build/runtime errors** at this moment (`compile_applet` and `lint_applet` both passed before the latest request).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running on port 3000 (`tsx server.ts`).\n- `/.gmp_cache/index.json` exists in workspace root \342\200\224 remember to clean up `/.gmp_cache` or leave ignored before finishing if temporary, after reading needed sub-skills.\n- Google Maps GHP API key was just provisioned in this session (`ProvisionMapsGhpKey` succeeded). Check how the key is exposed in `.env` / `process.env` (without echoing the secret!) and configure `vite.config.ts` / `.env.example` cleanly so `import.meta.env.VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` works in the browser.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Complete Mandatory Google Maps Grounding (BEFORE writing Maps code)**:\n   - View `/.gmp_cache/index.json` via `view_file`.\n   - Download & read matched sub-skills (especially **ToS compliance-review**, **React Maps JS / `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`**, and **Routes API**) into `/.gmp_cache/` with `?client=aistudio-agent`.\n   - Check which env var holds the provisioned Google Maps key (e.g., check file names in `/` or `grep -o \'^[A-Z0-9_]*=\' .env* 2>/dev/null`) so `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` is wired securely without hardcoding.\n   - Install `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` via a single `install_applet_package` call.\n2. **Backend Upgrades (`/server.ts`)**:\n   - Add `POST /api/travel/verify-vehicle`: Accepts `{ vehicleNumber?: string, photoBase64?: string, mimeType?: string }`. If a photo is provided, uses Gemini (`gemini-4-hydrogen` multimodal) to extract/read the registration plate & vehicle type from the photo! Validates registration format (Indian RTO state/RTO code/series + standard patterns), flags fake/tampered/malformed plate patterns honestly, and returns structured `{ normalizedNumber, vehicleType, stateRegion, formatValid, authenticityStatus, riskWarnings, summary, verifiedAt }` ready for real RTO/Vahan backend integration.\n   - Add `POST /api/sos/dispatch`: Automated backend-ready SOS dispatch endpoint accepting `{ userName, triggerSource, guardianContacts, policeNumber, latitude, longitude, vehicleNumber?, note? }` \342\200\224 logs & returns structured dispatch confirmation for Guardian + Police alerts & messages.\n   - Update `SAFETY_VOICE_TOOLS` & `buildSystemInstruction` in `/server.ts`:\n     - Update `share_live_location` to explicitly share live location with **BOTH registered guardians AND nearest police** (and handle phrases like \"share my location\" / \"share my business\").\n     - Ensure `activate_threat_mode` defaults `autoStartRecording: \'video\'` automatically.\n     - Add `open_lock_shield` and `verify_vehicle` / `open_travel_mode` voice commands so the entire app is controllable by voice.\n3. **Google Maps Live Route & Off-Route Deviation Engine (`/src/components/dashboard/TravelRouteMap.tsx` + `TravelModePanel.tsx` + `TravelModePage.tsx`)**:\n   - Build `TravelRouteMap.tsx` using `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` (`<APIProvider>`, `<Map mapId=\"DEMO_MAP_ID\" internalUsageAttributionIds={[\"gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\"]}>`, `AdvancedMarkerElement`, `useMapsLibrary(\'routes\')` \342\206\222 `Route.computeRoutes()` with fallback to Geocoding REST proxy if needed).\n   - Plot Start & Destination markers and the official Google Maps route polyline.\n   - Run real-time **Route Deviation Detection**: compute Haversine point-to-polyline distance from current GPS (`watchPosition`) to the Google Maps route path. If deviation > **200 meters** (or triggered via a clean \"Simulate Off-Route Test\" control for indoor/desktop verification):\n     - Trigger urgent audible warning tone + vibration + red **Route Deviation Alert Banner** (\"Vehicle moved off the Google Maps route by X meters!\").\n     - Automatically alert/prepare guardian message with live deviated GPS coordinates + offer 1-tap **Escalate to SOS & Call Guardian + Police**.\n   - Add **Vehicle / Auto Number Verification & Photo Capture** card inside `TravelModePage.tsx` (camera capture or photo upload + manual plate entry \342\206\222 calls `/api/travel/verify-vehicle` \342\206\222 saves verified vehicle number & photo thumbnail into `TravelSession` & Emergency History, and attaches vehicle info to guardian SMS/SOS alerts!).\n4. **Threat Mode Auto Continuous Audio + Video Recording (`/src/components/pages/ThreatModePage.tsx`)**:\n   - When Threat Mode activates (`threatSession.active` transitions to `true` or on activation button / AI voice command), **immediately and automatically start continuous Video + Audio recording** with NO extra confirmation step!\n   - If camera fails or is denied, automatically fall back to **continuous Audio-only recording** so recording always captures evidence.\n   - Show live pulsing **\"AUTO-RECORDING CONTINUOUSLY (Video + Audio)\"** status badge + live camera preview + auto-save on stop/deactivate into IndexedDB Evidence History.\n5. **Global Persistent AI Voice Controller (`/src/hooks/useGlobalVoiceController.ts` + `HomeDashboard.tsx` + `AiVoiceAssistantPage.tsx`)**:\n   - Lift the Gemini Live Voice WebSocket + REST command state out of `AiVoiceAssistantPage` into a persistent hook mounted in `HomeDashboard.tsx`, with a sleek compact **Floating Voice Controller Bar** when AI Voice is active on ANY page (`sos`, `threat`, `travel`, `nearby`, `history`, `home`)!\n   - Saying `\"Go to SOS\"`, `\"Activate Threat Mode\"`, `\"Share my location\"`, `\"Find nearby police\"`, `\"Open Travel Mode\"`, `\"Call both guardian and police\"` executes immediately while keeping Live Voice connected across page transitions!\n   - Make `share_live_location` share location to **BOTH Guardians AND Police** (displaying Guardian + Police live GPS share cards & SMS/call links on SOS page).\n6. **Automated SOS Call + Automated Message Dispatch (`EmergencyTriggerOverlay.tsx`, `HomeDashboard.tsx`, `SosPage.tsx`, `storage.ts`)**:\n   - When triggered by `\"Red Rose\"` secret voice code, 3x Shake, or 2x/3x Screen Tap (or Lock Shield), automatically call `/api/sos/dispatch` AND trigger `tel:` auto-call AND automatically trigger/queue emergency alert messages with GPS + vehicle number (if in Travel Mode) to ALL registered guardians AND surface Police (`100` / nearest AI station / `112`).\n7. **Google Maps Section 8 Case A Quota Defense (`src/main.tsx` + `src/App.tsx`)**:\n   - Add `window.gm_authFailure` + `OverQuotaMapError` console tap in `src/main.tsx` dispatching `\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'`.\n   - Render the required non-intrusive sticky amber quota banner in `src/App.tsx` when `\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'` fires.\n8. **Final Verification & Cleanup**:\n   - Remove `/.gmp_cache` temporary directory if not needed at runtime (or keep out of `dist`).\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in parallel.\n   - Call `restart_dev_server` so new `/server.ts` routes + Maps env var are live.\n   - Live-test `/api/health`, `/api/threat/nearby-police`, `/api/travel/verify-vehicle`, and `/api/sos/dispatch` via `curl`.\n   - Perform ToS Compliance Review check and include the mandatory **Google Maps Platform Required Response Verification Appendix** (Section 9) ONCE in the final response.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Google Maps Anti-Loop**: NEVER call `CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos`, `show_aistudio_ui` (`google_maps_setup`), or `ProvisionMapsGhpKey` again in this session!\n- **Google Maps Compliance**: Must read ToS compliance-review sub-skill, use `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`, `AdvancedMarkerElement`, `Route.computeRoutes()`, `internalUsageAttributionIds={[\"gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\"]}`, Case A quota banner, and append Section 9 Appendix once in the final message.\n- **No fabricated vehicle owner data or fake police numbers**: Be honest about plate format validation + AI photo OCR + backend RTO hookup point, and only show real grounded/OSM police numbers or `100` / `112`.\n- **OurSafe Design System**: Preserve botanical sage palette (`#CDD7C1` background, `#FCFDF9` cards, `#2F4526` deep olive primary, `Fraunces` + `Plus Jakarta Sans` + `JetBrains Mono`), zero demo/prototype labels, no `metadata.json` rename, no `window.alert`/`window.open`.\n</summary>"
