    skill_metadata {
      name: "securecoder-persona"
      description: "Enforces secure-by-default coding in AI Studio Build. On EVERY turn, follow 4 baseline rules directly without reading this file: (1) never hardcode API keys or credentials (keep private secrets like DB/Stripe/OAuth keys in server-side `process.env`, or follow runtime patterns like Android `BuildConfig`, Flutter `String.fromEnvironment`, or scoped public browser keys); (2) validate inputs and parameterize queries; (3) use safe framework bindings instead of raw HTML injection; (4) enforce server-side auth and access checks. Do NOT read this file for UI, styling, layout, client state, client-only features, or tasks covered solely by `gemini-api`, `gemini-interactions-api`, `firebase-integration-rpc`, or `cloudsql-setup`. Read this file ONLY when adding or modifying custom auth, databases, backend API routes, payments, OAuth, or untrusted HTML/URL handling beyond those skills, or when asked for a security review, audit, or vulnerability fix."
