  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Architecture Plan**\n\nI\'ve got the architecture plan nailed down, covering every user requirement completely. Now, I\'m diving deep into reviewing it meticulously. My focus is on ensuring the architecture is rock solid before writing any code. The goal is clean, complete, and production-ready code from the get-go.\n\n\n**Configuring Google Maps**\n\nI\'ve tackled the Google Maps API key configuration. I\'ve ensured secure and flexible key handling across development and production environments, specifically focusing on how Vite and environment variables interact for seamless key access. I\'ve also incorporated a fallback mechanism for robust key resolution. I\'m now looking at integrating the mandatory Section 8 Case A listener within `src/main.tsx`.\n\n\n**Addressing API Quota Errors**\n\nI\'m now implementing the quota error handling. I plan to dispatch a `\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'` event upon `gm_authFailure` and `OverQuotaMapError`/`QuotaExceededError` in the console. Then, in the `src/App.tsx`, I\'ll listen for this event, and display a non-blocking sticky amber banner. In the `TravelRouteMap.tsx`, I am explicitly overriding `internalUsageAttributionIds` per Section 4, using a modern `useMapsLibrary(\'routes\')` approach for route computation to avoid legacy methods. I\'ve also set explicit container dimensions.\n\n\n**Implementing Off-Route Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing real-time off-route deviation detection. I\'ve got a system for extracting path coordinates from route data. I want to build a solution to return routes that can be used to generate polylines containing `path`, `distanceMeters`, `durationMillis`, `viewport`, and `legs`. This will allow me to pinpoint a vehicle\'s deviation. I also want robust fallback messaging for API key issues.\n\n\n**Defining Travel Parameters**\n\nI\'m expanding the `LiveLocationShareSession` type with optional vehicle information, route details, and off-route alert flags. I\'m also adding police-sharing information like names and numbers for emergency scenarios. Now, I\'m focusing on building the `TravelRouteMap` component in `src/components/dashboard/TravelRouteMap.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Alert Escalation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the off-route alert escalation. I\'ll include an alert tone (if sound is enabled) and device vibration. A crimson banner will show, displaying the deviation. Alerts will be logged to Emergency History. It will trigger a `/api/sos/dispatch` notification option and display action buttons for the user to select from. I\'m also now rendering a pulsing Vehicle Location on the map.\n\n\n**Verifying Vehicle Information**\n\nI\'m now integrating vehicle verification into the system. This involves sending data to `/api/travel/verify-vehicle`, using Gemini to extract license plate details from photos. The server performs comprehensive RTO plate format validation, state code verification, and checks for suspicious patterns. The verified data, including a photo preview, is then saved in the active `TravelSession` and Emergency History, and included in all relevant messaging.\n\n\n**Implementing Threat Mode**\n\nI\'m now integrating an auto-recording system for Threat Mode. Upon activation, whether manual or AI-triggered, it instantly begins continuous video and audio recording using `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia`. I\'ve built in seamless fallback to audio-only recording if the camera is unavailable. The system ensures continuous safety recording is always running, regardless. I\'m also adding auto-checkpointing/saving to IndexedDB for evidence chunks.\n\n\n**Adding Threat Mode Indicators**\n\nI\'m now integrating live indicators and previews directly into the active Threat Mode view. A smooth deactivation process is also set, so when a user clicks *\"I\'m Safe \342\200\224 Deactivate\"*, the system will automatically stop the recording and neatly save the entire recording into Evidence History.\n\n**Introducing Global Voice Control**\n\nI\'m building a persistent AI voice controller using `src/hooks/useGlobalVoiceController.ts`, handling Gemini 3.8, live WebSocket, audio capture, 24kHz playback and the `/api/assistant/command` state at the HomeDashboard level. Navigating between SOS, Threat Mode, Travel Mode, Nearby, or History will not disconnect the voice session when AI Voice is on. I\'ll also add a floating global voice bar.\n\n\n**Defining Voice Commands**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI voice commands for quick actions. \"Go to SOS\" triggers an SOS alert, opens call panels, and dispatches automated calls and SMS. \"Activate Threat Mode\" starts recording and fetches nearby police numbers. \"Share location\" enables live location sharing to guardians and police. Other commands provide navigation and function access. I\'m focusing on seamless integration.\n\n\n**Triggering SOS Immediately**\n\nI\'m now implementing an immediate SOS dispatch upon trigger, like saying \"Red Rose\". I will build a secure `POST /api/sos/dispatch` in `/server.ts` for handling data, and it\'s already prepared for user backend SMS/Twilio/Firebase/Police webhook integration. I\'ve also set the default SOS trigger countdown to zero for instant alerts. It triggers with live GPS, guardian list, and police dispatch.\n\n\n"
