  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 3
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\nThe user requested the final production-ready frontend + backend-ready automation upgrades to **OurSafe** (AI-powered Women Safety Application \342\200\224 React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + Express + Gemini Live/Hydrogen + VitePWA + Capacitor Android native shield), specifically:\n1. **Threat Mode (\"Dread Mode\") Auto Continuous Video + Audio Recording**: Automatically start continuous video+audio recording the moment Threat Mode activates (zero extra confirmations; seamless fallback to continuous audio-only if camera unavailable), auto-saving to local IndexedDB Evidence History.\n2. **Travel Mode \342\200\224 Real Google Maps Two-Location Route + Real-Time Off-Route Deviation Alert**: Plot Start \342\206\222 Destination on real Google Maps (`@vis.gl/react-google-maps` + modern `Route.computeRoutes()`), watch live GPS (`watchPosition`), and trigger audible alarm + vibration + crimson deviation alert + Guardian SMS / SOS escalation if the vehicle deviates > 200m off the planned Google Maps route (plus a \"Test Off-Route Alert\" button for indoor/desktop testing).\n3. **Travel Mode \342\200\224 Auto / Cab Vehicle Number Verification + Photo Capture**: Verify registration number format (Indian RTO state/district/series + BH series) and optionally capture/upload a plate photo with AI OCR (`POST /api/travel/verify-vehicle`), flagging fake/suspicious plates honestly without fabricating owner data, and automatically attaching the vehicle number to Travel Mode & Guardian/Police SOS alerts.\n4. **Automated SOS Flow (\"Red Rose\" / 3x Shake / Screen Tap / Lock Shield)**: Immediate automated dispatch (`quickTriggerCountdownSec: 0` default) calling `POST /api/sos/dispatch` + automatic `tel:` dialer + automatic Guardian & Police alert messages with GPS + vehicle number.\n5. **Full-App Persistent Hands-Free AI Voice Control**: Keep Gemini 3.8 Live Voice active across ALL pages (`home`, `sos`, `threat`, `travel`, `assistant`, `nearby`, `history`) via a persistent global voice hook + floating top bar, supporting full voice navigation/automation (\"Go to SOS\", \"Activate Threat Mode\", \"Share my location\" / \"Share my business\" \342\206\222 shares live GPS to **BOTH Guardian AND Police**, \"Find police numbers\", \"Open Travel Mode\", \"Open Lock Shield\").\n6. **AI Nearby Police Station Numbers**: Verified 3-tier waterfall (Gemini Maps Grounding \342\206\222 Google Search Grounding \342\206\222 OpenStreetMap Nominatim) already live in `/server.ts`.\n7. **Final Quality Check**: Ensure all HTML/CSS, buttons, Google Maps, API routes, TypeScript compilation, linting, and security checks pass cleanly.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n\n#### All Code Changes COMPLETED (Not Yet Compiled/Linted/Restarted/Live-Tested)\n1. **Skills & Google Maps Grounding Completed**:\n   - Read `/skills/system_skills/google_maps_platform/SKILL.md` (complete).\n   - Read `/skills/system_skills/securecoder_persona/SKILL.md` (complete).\n   - Downloaded & read into `/.gmp_cache/`: `index.json`, `compliance-review.md` (ToS Compliance Filter reviewed!), `gmp-framework-react.md`, `routes-api-web-api.md`, `example_core.md`, `example_directions.md`, `example_routes.md`.\n   - Installed `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` via `install_applet_package`.\n   - Google Maps GHP API key was already provisioned earlier in this session (`ProvisionMapsGhpKey` succeeded, `setup_status: 1`). **NEVER call `show_aistudio_ui` (`google_maps_setup`) or any Maps provisioning RPC again!**\n2. **Core Config, Quota Defense & Types Modified**:\n   - `/.env.example`: Added `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=\"\"`.\n   - `/vite.config.ts`: Added `loadEnv` + `define: { \'import.meta.env.VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY\': JSON.stringify(...) }` falling back across `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` and `GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY`.\n   - `/src/main.tsx`: Added Section 8 Case A `window.gm_authFailure` + `console.error` tap for `OverQuotaMapError`/`QuotaExceededError` dispatching `\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'`.\n   - `/src/App.tsx`: Added root `\'gmp-quota-exceeded\'` listener rendering the required sticky amber top banner (`z-50`) and wired pre-login SOS triggers to `POST /api/sos/dispatch`.\n   - `/src/types/safety.ts`: Added `VehicleVerificationRecord`, extended `TravelSession` (`vehicleInfo`, `routeDistanceKm`, `routeDurationMin`, `offRouteAlertActive`, `offRouteDistanceMeters`) and `LiveLocationShareSession` (`sharedWithPolice`, `nearestPoliceName`, `nearestPolicePhone`).\n   - `/src/utils/storage.ts`: Updated `DEFAULT_PREFERENCES.quickTriggerCountdownSec` from `3` to `0` for immediate automated SOS dispatch.\n3. **Backend (`/server.ts`) Updated**:\n   - Expanded `SAFETY_VOICE_TOOLS` (`share_live_location` with `includePolice: true` including \"share my business\", `open_travel_mode`, `open_lock_shield`) and `buildSystemInstruction` for total hands-free voice control + auto-recording in Threat Mode.\n   - Increased JSON body limit to `6mb` for plate photo uploads.\n   - Updated `GET /api/health` to report `mapsKeyConfigured`.\n   - Added `POST /api/travel/verify-vehicle`: Validates inputs, runs optional Gemini `gemini-4-hydrogen` multimodal OCR on uploaded/captured plate photo, performs Indian RTO state/district/BH series format audit (`INDIAN_RTO_STATES`), and returns honest `format_verified` vs `suspicious_or_invalid` / `unrecognized` results with warnings.\n   - Added `POST /api/sos/dispatch`: Strictly validates inputs and logs/returns structured automated SOS dispatch confirmations for Guardians + Police + GPS + optional vehicle number.\n4. **New Frontend Modules Created**:\n   - `/src/hooks/useGlobalVoiceController.ts`: Persistent Gemini 3.8 Live WebSocket + 16kHz mic PCM stream + 24kHz speaker audio playback + REST `/api/assistant/command` hook mounted at `HomeDashboard` level.\n   - `/src/components/dashboard/TravelRouteMap.tsx`: Official `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` component (`APIProvider`, aliased `Map as GoogleMap`, `AdvancedMarker`, `Pin`, `useMap`, `useMapsLibrary(\'routes\')`, `mapId=\"DEMO_MAP_ID\"`, `internalUsageAttributionIds={[\'gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\']}`, explicit container height `h-[360px] sm:h-[420px]`), modern `Route.computeRoutes()` + `createPolylines()`, real-time `navigator.geolocation.watchPosition` point-to-polyline Haversine deviation detection (>200m threshold), audible alarm + vibration + crimson off-route alert banner + \"Test Off-Route Alert\" button + Case A Tier 2 quota detection.\n   - `/src/components/dashboard/VehicleVerificationCard.tsx`: Auto/cab registration input + camera/upload photo capture (`capture=\"environment\"`), calls `/api/travel/verify-vehicle`, displays RTO verification result & warnings, attaches vehicle to active `TravelSession`.\n5. **Existing Pages Updated**:\n   - `/src/components/pages/ThreatModePage.tsx`: Automatically starts continuous Video + Audio recording via `useEffect` whenever `threatSession.active` turns true (no manual confirmation!), automatically falls back to continuous Audio-only if camera fails, displays pulsing `\"AUTO-RECORDING CONTINUOUSLY\"` banner + live preview, and auto-saves to IndexedDB on stop/deactivate.\n   - `/src/components/dashboard/TravelModePanel.tsx`: Exposes `onDraftRouteChange` for live Google Maps preview, displays verified vehicle badge, attaches vehicle number to Guardian SMS.\n   - `/src/components/pages/TravelModePage.tsx`: Integrates `TravelModePanel` + `TravelRouteMap` + `VehicleVerificationCard` + Safety Check-In + Discreet Fake Call.\n   - `/src/components/pages/AiVoiceAssistantPage.tsx`: Refactored to consume persistent `voiceController` from `HomeDashboard` so voice never drops when switching screens.\n   - `/src/components/EmergencyTriggerOverlay.tsx`: Accepts optional `vehicleNumber`, attaches it to SMS, and reflects automated call + Guardian & Police message dispatch.\n   - `/src/components/pages/SosPage.tsx`: Upgraded Live Location Sharing card to share live GPS with **BOTH Guardians AND Police**, displaying instant Guardian SMS + Police SMS buttons when active.\n   - `/src/components/HomeDashboard.tsx`: Mounted `useGlobalVoiceController`, added persistent floating `\"Full-App AI Voice ON\"` banner when active on other pages, wired `POST /api/sos/dispatch` into `triggerSosAlert` and `handleToggleLiveLocationShare` (Guardian + Police), added `open_travel_mode` & `open_lock_shield` voice handlers, added `handleUpdateTravelVehicle` & `handleOffRouteAlert`, and wired all updated props.\n\n#### NOT YET EXECUTED (Verification & Cleanup Pending)\n- Have **NOT** yet removed temporary `/.gmp_cache` directory.\n- Have **NOT** yet run `compile_applet` or `lint_applet`.\n- Have **NOT** yet run `restart_dev_server` (needed so new `/server.ts` routes and Maps env var load).\n- Have **NOT** yet run `bun audit` (required by `securecoder-persona` because `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` was added to `package.json` and `bun.lock` exists).\n- Have **NOT** yet curl-tested `/api/health`, `/api/travel/verify-vehicle`, `/api/sos/dispatch`, and `/api/threat/nearby-police`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Google Maps Platform Compliance Rules Verified**:\n  - Used `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` exclusively (aliased `Map as GoogleMap` to prevent shadowing global `Map`).\n  - Zero deprecated APIs (`Marker`, `DirectionsService`, `DirectionsRenderer`, `Geocoder` JS class, `PlacesService` all avoided).\n  - Used `mapId=\"DEMO_MAP_ID\"` + `internalUsageAttributionIds={[\'gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\']}` (explicitly overriding `gmp_git_agentskills_v1`).\n  - Case A Quota Defense implemented (both Tier 1 in `src/main.tsx` + `src/App.tsx` sticky amber banner AND Tier 2 in `TravelRouteMap.tsx` catch block).\n  - Note: Check `TravelRouteMap.tsx` \342\200\224 `<Pin glyph=\"A\" />` vs `glyphText`: check TypeScript types of `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`\'s `<Pin>` component during `lint_applet`/`compile_applet` (if `Pin` expects `glyphText` or `glyph`, adjust cleanly!).\n- **Security Checks Applied (`securecoder-persona`)**:\n  - No hardcoded API keys anywhere; `GEMINI_API_KEY` stays server-side, `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` loaded from env.\n  - Strict input length, type, and MIME allowlist (`image/jpeg|image/png|image/webp`, max size check) on `/api/travel/verify-vehicle` and `/api/sos/dispatch`.\n  - Safe React JSX text bindings only (zero `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, zero unsafe `href`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- Earlier minor tool error: attempted to read `/src/components/dashboard/HomeDashboard.tsx` (actual path is `/src/components/HomeDashboard.tsx`); resolved immediately.\n- No build/lint/runtime errors yet on the new edits because compilation has not been run yet. Watch closely for any TypeScript type mismatch on `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`\'s `<Pin>` props (`glyph` vs `glyphText`) or `google.maps` global types (`@types/google.maps` is NOT installed in `package.json` \342\200\224 wait! Check `TravelRouteMap.tsx`: it references `google.maps.Polyline`, `google.maps.LatLng`, `google.maps.LatLngBounds` in TypeScript annotations! If `tsc --noEmit` flags `Cannot find namespace \'google\'`, either install `@types/google.maps` OR define minimal local TypeScript interfaces for the polyline/latLng objects so `tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors!).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Temporary directory `/.gmp_cache` currently exists in workspace root \342\200\224 remove it (`delete_dir` with `Force: true`) before final build so it doesn\'t clutter the workspace.\n- Dev server is still running the previous version of `server.ts`; call `restart_dev_server` after `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` pass so new endpoints and Maps env var are live.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (Execute Immediately in Order)\n1. **Clean up temporary cache**: Delete `/.gmp_cache` using `delete_dir` (`DirectoryPath: \"/.gmp_cache\"`, `Force: true`).\n2. **Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`** in parallel to check both Vite build and TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`).\n   - **Expected potential fix**: If `tsc --noEmit` reports `Cannot find namespace \'google\'` in `src/components/dashboard/TravelRouteMap.tsx` (or `<Pin glyph=...>` type error), fix cleanly in `TravelRouteMap.tsx` (use lightweight local TypeScript interfaces for `MapPolylineInstance` / `MapLatLng` / `MapLatLngBounds` or check `@vis.gl/react-google-maps`\'s exact `<Pin>` prop types) and re-run `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` together.\n3. **Run dependency security audit**: Run `bun audit` (read-only) via `run_command` since `bun.lock` exists and `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` was added.\n4. **Restart dev server**: Call `restart_dev_server` so updated `server.ts` and `vite.config.ts` env vars take effect.\n5. **Live smoke-test backend endpoints** via `run_command` (`curl`):\n   - `GET http://localhost:3000/api/health`\n   - `POST http://localhost:3000/api/travel/verify-vehicle` with `{\"vehicleNumber\":\"TN 09 AB 1234\"}` (should return `formatValid: true`, `Tamil Nadu`) AND with `{\"vehicleNumber\":\"ZZ 00 XX 0000\"}` (should return `authenticityStatus: \"suspicious_or_invalid\"`).\n   - `POST http://localhost:3000/api/sos/dispatch` with sample payload (should return `ok: true`, `policeNotified: true`).\n   - `POST http://localhost:3000/api/threat/nearby-police` with `{\"areaQuery\":\"Chennai\"}` (confirm still HTTP 200).\n6. **Verify `OurSafe` UI & send final user response**:\n   - Provide a concise, scannable summary of every completed feature + 2\342\200\2233 plain-language security safeguards bullets (from `securecoder-persona` Step 3, without internal jargon).\n   - **MANDATORY**: Append the **Google Maps Platform Required Response Verification Appendix** (Section 9 of `google_maps_platform/SKILL.md`) ONCE at the end of the final response!\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Google Maps Anti-Loop**: NEVER call `CheckMapsDemoKeyEligibilityAndTos`, `show_aistudio_ui` (`google_maps_setup`), or `ProvisionMapsGhpKey` again!\n- **Google Maps Required Response Appendix (Section 9 \342\200\224 MUST include ONCE in final message)**:\n  1. One-line confirmation that the Google Maps Platform ToS Compliance Review (`compliance-review`) sub-skill was reviewed.\n  2. Cost Notice: *\"Usage of Google Maps Platform products and services may incur costs against your Google Cloud project billing account.\"*\n  3. Products-Used List (bulleted, one per line):\n     - Maps JavaScript API (`@vis.gl/react-google-maps`, `AdvancedMarkerElement`)\n     - Routes API (`Route.computeRoutes()`)\n  4. API Key Restrictions link: `https://docs.cloud.google.com/api-keys/docs/add-restrictions-api-keys?utm_campaign=gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio`\n  5. License Scope: *\"Google-sourced code snippets are provided \'as-is\' under the Apache 2.0 License (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). This license covers only the Google-sourced snippets, not the full generated project output. The user is responsible for review and testing to ensure security and compliance with relevant Terms of Service.\"* (Note: Source-attribution comments N/A as code is agent-authored.)\n  6. ToS Link: *\"Use of this code is subject to the Google Maps Platform Terms of Service: https://cloud.google.com/maps-platform/terms?utm_campaign=gmp_mcp_codeassist_v1_aistudio\"* including regional Terms that apply based on billing address or user location (Prohibited Territories).\n- **Security Summary**: Include 2\342\200\2233 brief plain-language safeguard bullets (no internal security jargon).\n- **No `metadata.json` rename, no `window.alert`/`window.open`, no fabricated police numbers or fake vehicle owner names.**\n</summary>"
