  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Pinpointing the Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve homed in on the core of the issue \342\200\223 it\'s a direct consequence of two interacting lines of code within `/server.ts`. Line 1160, specifically, defines the `WebSocketServer` instantiation. I can now isolate and resolve the issue.\n\n\n**Isolating the Conflict**\n\nI\'ve discovered the root of the problem. It seems the `ws` library\'s upgrade listener is causing interference. It\'s aggressively rejecting WebSocket requests that don\'t match the specific path, `/api/live-voice`. Meanwhile, Vite\'s HMR mechanism, when `middlewareMode` is on without HMR disabled, attempts to connect to a WebSocket on a different port that is not accessible. This causes the client-side connection to fail outright. The fix should be contained to changes in `/server.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining HMR Configuration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to disable HMR correctly within the `server.ts` file. My goal is to prevent any conflict with the WebSocket server. I\'m considering using an environment variable, `DISABLE_HMR`, to conditionally set `hmr: false` within the Vite server configuration. This will enable correct behavior in the Cloud Run context. Alternatively, I am considering whether I can simply attach `hmr: {server}` to disable HMR when necessary.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "IhsDa4LCEv3Q_uMPmY3oAQ"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5660955858844155562"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Use noServer mode for the /api/live-voice WebSocket bridge and disable Vite middlewareMode HMR WebSocket to eliminate @vite/client WebSocket closed without opened errors\", \"Instruction\":\"Switch WebSocketServer to noServer with an explicit /api/live-voice upgrade handler and set hmr: false in createViteServer middlewareMode options in server.ts\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":1163, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  // Real-Time Gemini 3.8 Live API WebSocket Bridge\\n  const wss = new WebSocketServer({ noServer: true });\\n\\n  server.on(\'upgrade\', (request, socket, head) => {\\n    const reqUrl = new URL(request.url || \'/\', `http://${request.headers.host || \'localhost\'}`);\\n    if (reqUrl.pathname === \'/api/live-voice\') {\\n      wss.handleUpgrade(request, socket, head, (ws) => {\\n        wss.emit(\'connection\', ws, request);\\n      });\\n    } else {\\n      socket.destroy();\\n    }\\n  });\", \"StartLine\":1158, \"TargetContent\":\"  // Real-Time Gemini 3.8 Live API WebSocket Bridge\\n  const wss = new WebSocketServer({ server, path: \'/api/live-voice\' });\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":1338, \"ReplacementContent\":\"    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true, hmr: false },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\", \"StartLine\":1332, \"TargetContent\":\"    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Fixing Vite HMR and WebSocket upgrade handling\", \"toolSummary\":\"Fix Vite HMR WebSocket error in server.ts\"}"
