  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Client**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `@vite/client` code, specifically lines 938-947. I see the hardcoded HMR port (24678) and the websocket connection logic using `import.meta.url`. I\'m starting to understand how the client establishes its connection.\n\n\n**Investigating the Configuration**\n\nI\'m now digging into the configuration merging logic within Vite, specifically focusing on how `vite.config.ts` interacts with inline configurations passed to `createViteServer`. The mystery remains: why does the hardcoded HMR port persist even when HMR is explicitly disabled? I\'m examining the precedence rules, suspecting that `vite.config.ts` might be overriding the inline setting or that `VitePWA` is affecting the HMR setting. I need to understand why the `@vite/client` code is still being loaded even when HMR is set to false.\n\n\n"
