  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Vite\'s Quirks**\n\nI\'ve made a key discovery: Vite 8\'s behavior with WebSockets is nuanced. Specifically, `ws: false` in `vite@8.3.0` completely disables the WebSocket server, which is distinct from simply disabling HMR. Furthermore, even with `hmr: false`, Vite 8 still attaches `@vite/client`! This insight could lead to significant optimizations and simpler configurations.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "NhwDa4WoGeLHsOIPh-O2qQQ"
