  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering the Connection**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I just realized a key link. Lines 1020 and 938 of `/@vite/client` show `hmrPort = 24678` and connection via `createHMRHandler`. This is because Vite 8\'s `server.ts` establishes a Vite server in `middlewareMode: true` AND `viteConfig`.\n\n\n**Analyzing the HMR Logic**\n\nI\'m now digging into the heart of the HMR issue. I\'ve found `vite.config.ts` controls HMR behavior with `DISABLE_HMR`. I\'m trying to determine why `hmrPort = 24678` is still present, even with HMR seemingly disabled. Specifically, I\'m checking the interaction between `restart_dev_server`, `DISABLE_HMR`, and Vite\'s server creation, particularly when `middlewareMode` is true and HMR is set to false. Is the transformation of `index.html` injecting client code no matter what, and connecting regardless of options?\n\n\n**Unveiling the Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve made a crucial discovery. Even with HMR and WS explicitly disabled in `middlewareMode`, Vite *still* injects the client script and attempts to connect to port 24678. The culprit is the default `hmrPort` assignment when no specific server instance is provided in `vite.config.ts`. Cloud Run\'s port restrictions make this a dead end. I\'m now testing the explicit disabling of both HMR and WS to confirm this behavior.\n\n\n"
