  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Vite 8 Code**\n\nI\'ve been poring over Vite 8\'s codebase, specifically line 17233 in `node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js`. The focus is now on how `wsConfig` and `isWsServerSpecified` are handled within the server configuration, especially in middleware mode. I\'m trying to see what might cause issues.\n\n\n**Uncovering a Critical Bug**\n\nI\'ve made a crucial discovery in Vite 8\'s behavior. When running in middleware mode with `ws` or `hmr` set to false, Vite injects the client script regardless. This script then attempts an unconditional WebSocket connection to port 24678, leading to errors in the browser console. The fix is either to ensure `ws: { server }` is passed or to correctly handle the upgrade event when using a custom server.\n\n\n**Investigating HMR and WS**\n\nI\'m now focusing on HMR and WebSocket interactions. I\'ve realized we can resolve the connection issue. If `isWsServerSpecified` is true and `hmrPort` becomes null, the browser will connect correctly via `wss://` on port 443, which the container routes to 3000! Moreover, our `server.on(\'upgrade\')` specifically handles Vite\'s \"vite-hmr\" WebSocket cleanly on that same port, which is perfect and avoids socket destruction, hence we will avoid error!\n\n\n"
