  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Vite 8 Deprecation**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on a deprecation notice within Vite 8. I\'ve pinpointed specific lines related to the server configuration and WebSocket usage. It appears the older `server.hmr.protocol/host/port/path/clientPort/timeout/server` options are being phased out in favor of `server.ws.*`. The update suggests that when `ws: { server }` is passed to `createViteServer`, it is the modern configuration path.\n\n\n**Investigating Upgrade Listener Changes**\n\nI\'ve discovered Vite 8 directly attaches its WebSocket upgrade listener to the Express HTTP server, specifically port 3000, which is a key change. Configuration settings in `vite.config.ts` are still controlling HMR and watching, and I need to verify how. Specifically, I am digging into how Vite\'s upgrade handler interacts with our `/api/live-voice` path, and how that is affected by the `DISABLE_HMR` environment variable being set. I\'m going to update `/server.ts` and test this.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "QB0Da8-AO8HH-sAPgILg0Ag"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_2431338765714455305"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Attach Vite 8 dev WebSocket directly to the Express HTTP server on port 3000 and let non-/api/live-voice upgrades pass through to Vite\", \"Instruction\":\"Remove socket.destroy() for non-/api/live-voice upgrades and pass ws: { server } to createViteServer in server.ts\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":1172, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  server.on(\'upgrade\', (request, socket, head) => {\\n    const reqUrl = new URL(request.url || \'/\', `http://${request.headers.host || \'localhost\'}`);\\n    if (reqUrl.pathname === \'/api/live-voice\') {\\n      wss.handleUpgrade(request, socket, head, (ws) => {\\n        wss.emit(\'connection\', ws, request);\\n      });\\n    }\\n  });\", \"StartLine\":1160, \"TargetContent\":\"  server.on(\'upgrade\', (request, socket, head) => {\\n    const reqUrl = new URL(request.url || \'/\', `http://${request.headers.host || \'localhost\'}`);\\n    if (reqUrl.pathname === \'/api/live-voice\') {\\n      wss.handleUpgrade(request, socket, head, (ws) => {\\n        wss.emit(\'connection\', ws, request);\\n      });\\n    } else {\\n      socket.destroy();\\n    }\\n  });\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":1349, \"ReplacementContent\":\"    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true, ws: { server } },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\", \"StartLine\":1341, \"TargetContent\":\"    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true, hmr: false, ws: false },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Attaching Vite 8 WebSocket to Express server\", \"toolSummary\":\"Configure Vite server.ws on Express server\"}"
