  planner_response {
    response: "Fixed the `[vite] Error: WebSocket closed without opened.` runtime error.\n\n### Root Cause & Fix\n- **Root Cause:** In Vite middleware mode, Vite defaulted its dev WebSocket client to port `24678` (unreachable behind port `3000`), and the `/api/live-voice` WebSocket server was attached directly to the HTTP server in a way that rejected non-`/api/live-voice` upgrade requests.\n- **Fix:**\n  - Switched the Gemini Live Voice WebSocket bridge to manual upgrade routing (`noServer: true`) so it only intercepts `/api/live-voice` upgrades.\n  - Attached Vite\'s dev WebSocket (`server.ws.server`) directly to the main Express HTTP server on port `3000`, removing the unreachable `:24678` connection target while keeping `DISABLE_HMR` controls intact.\n\n### Verification\n- Build compilation and TypeScript type-checking (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- Confirmed live after server restart that `hmrPort` resolves to `null` (using the main app host/port) and both the Vite dev WebSocket and `/api/live-voice` WebSocket open cleanly."
    message_id: "4R0Da7DhDt6939IPzoTWqQs"
    modified_response: "Fixed the `[vite] Error: WebSocket closed without opened.` runtime error.\n\n### Root Cause & Fix\n- **Root Cause:** In Vite middleware mode, Vite defaulted its dev WebSocket client to port `24678` (unreachable behind port `3000`), and the `/api/live-voice` WebSocket server was attached directly to the HTTP server in a way that rejected non-`/api/live-voice` upgrade requests.\n- **Fix:**\n  - Switched the Gemini Live Voice WebSocket bridge to manual upgrade routing (`noServer: true`) so it only intercepts `/api/live-voice` upgrades.\n  - Attached Vite\'s dev WebSocket (`server.ws.server`) directly to the main Express HTTP server on port `3000`, removing the unreachable `:24678` connection target while keeping `DISABLE_HMR` controls intact.\n\n### Verification\n- Build compilation and TypeScript type-checking (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- Confirmed live after server restart that `hmrPort` resolves to `null` (using the main app host/port) and both the Vite dev WebSocket and `/api/live-voice` WebSocket open cleanly."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
