  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Attributes**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the four generated images; they are exceptional. I\'m focusing on the paths that were returned, specifically `/src/assets/images/women_safety_hero_17`. The integration of the color palette is remarkable!\n\n\n**Prioritizing Image Placement**\n\nI\'ve got the images laid out now: a hero banner first, then cards for voice, safe commute, and guardian network, followed by the emblem and home banner. I\'m moving on to Phase 2 of the implementation: \"OurSafe\" voice wake with a greeting and full-app voice control. I\'m focusing on a dedicated utility for a reliable spoken greeting.\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Assistant**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the voice assistant implementation. I\'ve defined the greeting: \"OurSafe app is here, how can I help you?\". I\'m ensuring it uses a clear female English voice. I\'m focusing on seamless integration, triggering voice command capture immediately after the greeting ends, using a timeout fallback. I\'ve also added the `cancelAssistantSpeech()` function.\n\n\n**Expanding Voice Commands**\n\nI\'m expanding the voice command system to ensure functionality even with potential Gemini Live WebSocket issues. I\'ve integrated a robust suite of commands for immediate app control: `\"deactivate threat\"`, `\"travel mode\"`, and others. My next step involves upgrading the `useEmergencyQuickTriggers.ts` hook.\n\n\n**Designing Voice Interaction**\n\nI\'m working on the user experience when \"OurSafe\" is detected. I\'ll trigger the chime and `onWakeWordDetected`. I\'m focused on a sleek visual pop-up, `/src/components/OurSafeVoiceWakeBanner.tsx`, that appears immediately, even over the lock shield, like a Google Assistant interface. The pop-up will display a waveform, greeting, live status, and user transcript, with quick command chips for easy access.\n\n\n**Refining Voice Integration**\n\nI\'m now refining the voice interaction. The system immediately greets the user, then activates Gemini Live Voice, or a fallback if offline. If a command is uttered simultaneously, it\'s executed, confirming it aloud. I\'m upgrading `HomeDashboard.tsx` to handle the `OurSafeVoiceWakeBanner` state, ensuring smooth transitions and responsiveness. I\'m focusing on the user experience.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Voice Response**\n\nI\'m making sure that when the wake word is detected, I immediately close any blocking elements and open the `OurSafeVoiceWakeBanner`. I\'m speaking the greeting and starting the live voice session. I\'m focusing on instant command execution if one was already spoken, and the suspension of `quickTriggers` during the greeting to prevent a loop.\n\n\n**Enhancing Android Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating \"Open guardians\" as a voice command, and I\'m updating `OurSafeBackgroundShieldService.kt` to make sure even locked phones or different apps will hear me say `\"OurSafe app is here, how can I help you?\"` when they utter `\"OurSafe\"` or `\"House Safe\"`, and bring `MainActivity` to the foreground. Also, I will update `server.ts` to improve Gemini Live\'s wake word recognition.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Visual Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on visually structuring the `HomeAboutPage.tsx`. First things first, I\'m ensuring there\'s a strong visual impact with a well-chosen image. After that, I\'ll move on to implementing the other features. I\'m aiming for a clean, editorial look with measured elements and single-elevation cards. I\'m adding a referrer policy, and styling the fallback containers.\n\n\n**Designing Hero Presentation**\n\nI\'ve just added a full-width, editorial visual (`women_safety_hero_1795440817803.jpg`) at the top, styled for impact. It\'s a 16:9 ratio with rounded corners and a bottom scrim for the caption. I\'ve placed a caption and buttons, including one to trigger the voice assistant, and a secondary one to open the SOS function. I\'m prioritizing the presentation for immediate user engagement.\n\n\n"
