  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Synchronizing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on updating `/src/components/HomeDashboard.tsx` and `/src/components/pages/HomeAboutPage.tsx` concurrently. Specifically, I\'m carefully verifying the imports and function calls, making sure that `OurSafeVoiceWakeBanner` and the voice assistant functions are correctly incorporated. The parallel updates require careful attention to detail.\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Interactions**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating voice commands and responses. I\'ve added a contacts feature with `open_contacts` and defined states for a voice wake sheet, handling the greeting, listening, and execution phases. The `handleVoiceSheetCommand` function now prioritizes immediate execution with `parseInstantVoiceIntent` for local commands and uses `voiceController.runTextCommand` for broader interpretation. Also, I\'ve updated the `handleWakeWordDetected` function to prioritize app presentation.\n\n\n**Refining Voice Greeting Logic**\n\nI\'m currently refining the greeting logic within the voice interaction flow. Now, if a follow-up command is immediately detected, it gets executed right away, and a message confirms that the app is handling the command. Otherwise, the app greets the user and immediately starts listening for commands using `startLiveVoice`. I\'ve also updated the `useEmergencyQuickTriggers` to suspend the component when the voice wake sheet is open.\n\n\n**Optimizing Trigger Behavior**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the trigger behavior when the voice wake banner closes. The `quickTriggers` listening resumes seamlessly, avoiding microphone collisions between Gemini Live or the Banner. I\'m also ensuring `autoStartVoice` calls `handleWakeWordDetected`, prompting the \"How can I help you?\" message and opening the banner. I\'m also updating the UI to render `<OurSafeVoiceWakeBanner ... />` above the voice orb, hiding the orb when the banner is open to prevent overlap. Finally, I need to add the hero section with the women\'s safety hero photography to `HomeAboutPage.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Home Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now designing the hero section for the home page, aiming for a crisp headline: \"Walk Every Street With Confidence.\" I\'m including a clean kicker: \"OurSafe Women\'s Safety Companion \302\267 Voice-Controlled 24/7 Protection\" and a primary call to action, \"Say \'OurSafe\' \342\200\224 Hear Voice Assistant,\" that triggers the `onWakeVoice` function, along with an \"Open SOS\" button. I\'m focusing on directness and clarity.\n\n\n"
